1
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:07,980
Players of the Deathmatch,
please gather in the main hall.

2
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,550
(Survival means a sign of strength.)

3
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,850
I'm going to take that shirt from you.

4
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,660
It felt weird, going into the Deathmatch.

5
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,230
Both Xitsuh and I...

6
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:27,230
had history with Team P2.

7
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:30,230
We were together for an entire season.

8
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:33,130
Team P3 is the biggest threat
when it comes to games.

9
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:35,670
But we were the closest to them.

10
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,570
I've known Xitsuh and Jin Ho
from the second season.

11
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:38,770
And we're close.

12
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:42,210
I admire Seong Beom and Hye Seon too.

13
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:46,080
The fact that we had to go up against them
for our own survival...

14
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,220
didn't make me happy.

15
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:50,750
I have a lot on my mind.

16
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:54,320
I wanted to go up against one of the teams
from the alliance we had a beef with.

17
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:56,620
I didn't want to go up against Team P2.

18
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,530
I consider Jin Hyeong
to be the strongest player...

19
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:02,460
when it comes to Deathmatches.

20
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:06,230
Team P2? They won't be easy to beat.

21
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:08,500
We're one player short.

22
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:11,670
I thought Team P3 was intimidating
and hard to beat.

23
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:14,380
I felt that
this Deathmatch wouldn't be easy.

24
00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:19,080
Team P2. Team P3.

25
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:23,480
You must participate in
the 1-on-1 team Deathmatch.

26
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:26,920
The entire losing team of the Deathmatch
will be eliminated.

27
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:31,290
The winning team will have to survive
on the outdoor survival grounds.

28
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:37,500
Today's Deathmatch will be revealed now.

29
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:40,440
Today's Deathmatch is...

30
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:42,970
(Brutal Morning Commute)

31
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:45,940
Brutal Morning Commute.

32
00:01:46,170 --> 00:01:47,240
"BMC?"

33
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:48,810
In this game of Brutal Morning Commute,

34
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:51,180
players must car-shaped tiles
on the board...

35
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:53,250
in order to bring...

36
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,980
your team's car tiles out of the board.

37
00:01:56,480 --> 00:02:00,220
The game will proceed on a square board...

38
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:02,790
that consists of 14 rows and 14 columns.

39
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:06,790
There are neutral car tiles
that can be moved...

40
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,360
and fixed object tiles on the board.

41
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:13,600
In the center of the game board,
eight starting spots are...

42
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,500
already designated
for each team's car tiles.

43
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,010
Before the game begins,
the team that goes second...

44
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:22,910
will decide where the three
of their opposing car tiles go.

45
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:24,650
Afterward, the team going first...

46
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:28,320
will pick the spot
for their last car tile.

47
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:30,150
By default, the four car tiles...

48
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:32,790
of the team going second
will fill in the remaining spots.

49
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:36,490
Once the game begins,
players from each team...

50
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:39,260
will go head-to-head
based on the established order.

51
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:42,330
The rest of the players
cannot communicate...

52
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:44,730
with the players currently in-game.

53
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:47,470
The players currently in-game...

54
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:50,940
will take turns to play the game.

55
00:02:51,770 --> 00:02:56,010
Car tiles can be moved in a straight line
until they are blocked...

56
00:02:56,210 --> 00:02:57,880
by another car tile or a fixed object.

57
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:00,950
Players are allowed to move...

58
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:03,920
their team's car tiles
or neutral car tiles.

59
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:05,920
But they're not allowed to move...

60
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:09,420
the opposing team's car tile or a car tile
that was moved in the previous turn.

61
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:12,060
Each team's car tile...

62
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:15,560
can leave the game board
once it hits the edge.

63
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,270
Players currently in-game...

64
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:21,700
will have one minute each.

65
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:26,210
The timer will be active
during the player's own turn.

66
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:29,080
But the timer will pause...

67
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,910
during their opponent's turn.

68
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:34,750
As long as their minute isn't up,

69
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,980
they can proceed with multiple turns.

70
00:03:37,690 --> 00:03:41,160
Once their time is up,
they must switch with a new player...

71
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:44,160
within the team
even if their opponent's time isn't up.

72
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:46,890
All players are required...

73
00:03:46,890 --> 00:03:49,560
to play at least a turn
once they're in the game.

74
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:53,570
If players don't move a car tile
even once during the one minute,

75
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,370
their opponent will get the turn.

76
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:00,740
If necessary, each team will request...

77
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:03,040
a timeout only once.

78
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:07,550
During the timeout, everyone on the team
can freely communicate.

79
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,450
The first team that removes...

80
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:13,650
three out of the four car tiles
from the board...

81
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:15,920
will be the surviving team
of the Deathmatch.

82
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,230
(Survived)

83
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:21,500
Brutal Morning Commute will begin shortly.

84
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:25,570
Each team is to come up
with their player lineup.

85
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:29,800
To put it simply, it's a puzzle game.

86
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,570
Let's say I want to move something.

87
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:34,440
I have to keep making space...

88
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,480
with other tiles while moving them around.

89
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:39,650
This might be closer
to reading the board and the player...

90
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,520
rather than calculating possibilities.

91
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:44,990
So it's like... "How many steps
must I be ahead? What should I do now?"

92
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:48,120
Given the nature
of tactical piece-movement games,

93
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:51,230
we must be able to read them
at least three moves ahead.

94
00:04:51,490 --> 00:04:53,430
Reading their moves is very important.

95
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:56,030
Gosh, with the lineup,

96
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:00,130
we were forced to play on our own.

97
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:01,870
That made things complicated.

98
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:05,810
I had a feeling that
we would have a shot with this game.

99
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:09,180
With more people, things could get
more confusing and complicated.

100
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:12,810
I thought we might have an upper hand
since we were a smaller team.

101
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:15,850
Team P3 ranked 4th in the Money Challenge.

102
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:17,650
They will decide to go 1st or 2nd.

103
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:20,760
(Going 1st, going 2nd)

104
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:24,390
The team going 2nd can pick 3 spots
for their opponent's car tiles.

105
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:29,600
The team going 1st can pick 1 spot
for their own car tile.

106
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,800
And the remaining four spots
will be filled...

107
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:35,070
with the car tiles
of the team going second.

108
00:05:35,070 --> 00:05:36,700
(The remaining 4 spots will be filled
with the car tiles of the team going 2nd.)

109
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:39,570
Each team will have ten minutes
to strategize...

110
00:05:39,710 --> 00:05:42,040
and then submit the player lineup.

111
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,910
We can decide to go either 1st or 2nd.

112
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:48,120
If we were to go second,
which spots would we choose?

113
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,820
If we were to go first,
which spot will we take?

114
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:54,690
Getting this one out will be super tough.

115
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:57,790
Right. These two will be tough.

116
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:00,460
It's better to pick their spots...

117
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:02,500
at the expense of losing a turn.

118
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:05,070
We should go 2nd
and give them the 3 worst spots.

119
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:06,970
- Picking three spots?
- That might be better.

120
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:11,570
We should calculate the lowest number
of turns each car needs to escape.

121
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:13,870
Giving them the cars
with the highest numbers sounds good.

122
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:17,810
People might think all cars have
the same chance of making it out.

123
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:19,450
When we calculated the moves,

124
00:06:19,610 --> 00:06:22,850
some of the locations were
more difficult to extract the cars.

125
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:25,850
As for this one, we just need to move
these two cars to extract it.

126
00:06:25,850 --> 00:06:27,290
It's relatively easy.

127
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:29,190
Right. That's why I think...

128
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:31,360
they will go second, so they can end up...

129
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,560
- with easier cars to extract.
- So they'll go second?

130
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,200
They'll definitely go second.

131
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:36,630
Of course. I think so too.

132
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:38,470
Being able to designate the cars...

133
00:06:38,470 --> 00:06:40,300
looks like a huge advantage.

134
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:44,070
Let's say we use up the whole minute
just for one turn.

135
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,810
But that doesn't allow them
to have more turns.

136
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:47,480
- They can take only one turn as well.
- That's right.

137
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:49,380
Compared to us, Jin Hyeong is better
at this kind of game...

138
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:51,180
and has better understanding.

139
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:53,580
We can rotate among the three of us.

140
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,580
- You'll end up playing a lot more.
- Right.

141
00:06:55,850 --> 00:06:59,190
If I'm not sure, I'll only move one tile.

142
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:00,220
Then he'll go again.

143
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,860
- If I'm confused, I'll play my turn...
- Yes. Just...

144
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,190
- to prevent them from scoring.
- Take your time.

145
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:05,590
If you're confused,
just focus on preventing them.

146
00:07:05,790 --> 00:07:08,260
- No need to rush. Let's play it safe.
- Right.

147
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:10,230
- We can do this all day.
- Right.

148
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:11,270
Yes.

149
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:14,070
As for games like this,
you don't have a better chance...

150
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,500
at winning because you have more people
on your team.

151
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:18,040
It could backfire.

152
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:20,440
Too many cooks spoil the broth.

153
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:24,180
Having one clear leader
could give us an edge in this game.

154
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:27,520
We decided to move only one piece
if we weren't sure of what to do.

155
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,980
But if we saw a way to extract cars,

156
00:07:30,150 --> 00:07:31,520
we could push for it.

157
00:07:31,590 --> 00:07:33,290
Here's one more thing to remember.
We can get in their way...

158
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:34,920
with the neutral car tiles
as well as our own car tiles.

159
00:07:35,090 --> 00:07:36,760
For example, the bottom one is theirs,
and the one on top is ours.

160
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,990
If we move down our car,
this car won't be able to get out.

161
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:43,060
They won't be able to extract their car
until our car is removed.

162
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,530
- Right.
- We can prevent them with our tiles too.

163
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,870
Both teams can move the neutral cars.

164
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,140
But only we can move our team tiles.

165
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:54,010
I wanted us to block
at least one of their cars with our car.

166
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,880
Your time to strategize is over.

167
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:59,680
Please submit the player lineup.

168
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:02,150
(YunB, Ha Seung Jin, Lee Jin Hyeong)

169
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:04,990
(Xitsuh, Hong Jin Ho,
Heo Seong Beom, Choi Hye Seon)

170
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:08,190
Team P3 ranked 4th in the Money Challenge.

171
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:09,920
They will decide to go 1st or 2nd.

172
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,360
We'll go second.

173
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:14,660
Team P2 will go 1st.

174
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:17,300
Team P3 will go 2nd.

175
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:20,800
Team P3, as you're going 2nd,
please place 3 red car tiles...

176
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,040
in the center of the board.

177
00:08:26,770 --> 00:08:28,680
We gave them the spots that
would make car extraction tough...

178
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:30,180
if we were to have them.

179
00:08:31,850 --> 00:08:33,350
(They finish placing 3 red cars.)

180
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:37,080
Team P2, as you are going 1st,
place 1 red tile on the board.

181
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:41,260
The three of us were thinking
which spot to take.

182
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:47,430
Two of our cars were placed
in a way that they could be extracted...

183
00:08:47,430 --> 00:08:49,630
in the same direction.
That could be a good thing.

184
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,370
But if one side of the board is blocked,

185
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,570
we won't be able to extract them together.

186
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,640
I thought this would be a tough one.

187
00:08:57,710 --> 00:08:59,910
Let's look for spots
where both directions could work.

188
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:03,280
Let's say we want to be conservative
and focus on defense.

189
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:06,280
- We could pick this and move it here.
- Okay.

190
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:08,380
We can block them going out through here.

191
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,720
- Right.
- If we start with that,

192
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:12,020
we'll be able to trap them.

193
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:13,920
That's a good idea. Okay.

194
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,290
(Team P2 picks the spot
for their last car.)

195
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:21,300
Yellow tiles will be assigned
to the unchosen spots.

196
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:26,230
(The initial placement)

197
00:09:26,430 --> 00:09:28,400
The game will begin now.

198
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:30,870
Good game.

199
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:32,510
Good luck.

200
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:34,910
Team P2 will begin.

201
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,240
Please move a car tile.

202
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:39,350
(YunB)

203
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:51,660
(YunB blocks the yellow car
with their red car.)

204
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,260
It's Team P3's turn.

205
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:57,530
(Xitsuh)

206
00:09:57,630 --> 00:10:00,630
I thought I might have an easier time
to extract cars from this side.

207
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:04,370
Before the game, I wanted to make
car extraction harder on this side.

208
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:06,470
Moving a bus tile to the right...

209
00:10:06,470 --> 00:10:09,010
would complicate the whole side.

210
00:10:09,110 --> 00:10:10,410
I didn't want to make it easy for them.

211
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:11,810
It's Team P2's turn.

212
00:10:11,810 --> 00:10:14,450
(YunB)

213
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,450
Be careful from now on.
Wait. I can't talk.

214
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:18,590
- Communication isn't allowed.
- I'm sorry.

215
00:10:19,350 --> 00:10:22,360
During this game,
we can't give each other advice.

216
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:26,190
So individual performance
will play a crucial role.

217
00:10:27,390 --> 00:10:29,860
Exchanging information
will be very difficult.

218
00:10:30,430 --> 00:10:32,100
We have no choice
but to believe in the active player.

219
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:39,970
(YunB)

220
00:10:39,970 --> 00:10:41,280
You have ten seconds left.

221
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,750
In this game, it's not about
who plays better offense...

222
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:46,450
and gets the cars out first.

223
00:10:46,450 --> 00:10:49,780
It's more important not to make mistakes
in this kind of game.

224
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:52,450
When mistakes build up,

225
00:10:52,450 --> 00:10:54,460
you're bound to lose.

226
00:10:54,590 --> 00:10:57,860
We thought giving more turns to one person
put us ahead of the game.

227
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:00,090
(YunB)

228
00:11:00,090 --> 00:11:01,500
Your time is up.

229
00:11:02,030 --> 00:11:03,100
Please switch.

230
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:06,500
(YunB of Team P2 switches
with Ha Seung Jin.)

231
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:11,070
It's Team P2's turn.

232
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:14,140
(Ha Seung Jin)

233
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,380
I think this is the right strategy.

234
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:17,140
- Instead of...
- In the beginning, yes.

235
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:18,580
- We can't overdo it.
- Right.

236
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,210
We don't know what everyone's thinking.

237
00:11:20,710 --> 00:11:23,220
I thought every move mattered.

238
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:26,650
I tried to see if there were
other variables by moving a car.

239
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:29,820
I tried to check every angle
within that minute and to be careful.

240
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:35,030
(Ha Seung Jin)

241
00:11:37,430 --> 00:11:39,000
It's Team P3's turn.

242
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,170
(Xitsuh)

243
00:11:40,170 --> 00:11:45,510
(Xitsuh opens up the western route.)

244
00:11:45,570 --> 00:11:47,070
- Right.
- We can block this one.

245
00:11:47,570 --> 00:11:49,680
- We can get these two cars out...
- That one might be better.

246
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:51,510
as long as we have our turns.

247
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:52,910
This one is trapped.

248
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,320
- We can extract this once it's moved.
- Right.

249
