moving the cars away in that section.

501
00:23:58,740 --> 00:23:59,770
Your time is up.

502
00:23:59,770 --> 00:24:02,480
(Lee Jin Hyeong of Team P2 switches
with YunB.)

503
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:06,750
We're very close to extracting one car.

504
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:08,580
- This one made it to this spot.
- Okay.

505
00:24:08,850 --> 00:24:11,920
But they can't touch our car.

506
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:14,350
If we try to free up the east side,
they're going to get in our way.

507
00:24:14,490 --> 00:24:16,720
If we keep trying to free up this side,
they're bound to make a mistake.

508
00:24:18,930 --> 00:24:21,260
- Help us get out.
- It's Team P3's turn.

509
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:23,830
Come on.

510
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:25,370
- Let's do this forever.
- It's Team P2's turn.

511
00:24:25,370 --> 00:24:26,500
We'll do it until tomorrow.

512
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:29,400
This game comes down
to who messes up first.

513
00:24:29,470 --> 00:24:31,040
When we make only the necessary moves,

514
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:33,240
the defensive pressure
will never come to an end.

515
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,710
That's why Xitsuh and I...

516
00:24:34,710 --> 00:24:36,680
were in this crazy,
relentless defensive battle.

517
00:24:38,650 --> 00:24:39,850
Your time is up.

518
00:24:40,310 --> 00:24:45,590
(Xitsuh of Team P3 switches
with Hong Jin Ho.)

519
00:24:45,850 --> 00:24:47,250
It's Team P3's turn.

520
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:50,420
What happened here?

521
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:12,480
It's Team P2's turn.

522
00:25:16,620 --> 00:25:17,820
Darn it.

523
00:25:20,250 --> 00:25:24,020
(Team P2 extracts their 1st car.)

524
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:25,260
Darn it.

525
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:31,200
I messed up.

526
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:33,270
It's Team P3's turn.

527
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:35,170
I made a ridiculous mistake.

528
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:38,740
It was my turn.
I went up and looked at the board.

529
00:25:38,740 --> 00:25:41,410
It was a bit confusing to read the board
after three turns.

530
00:25:41,470 --> 00:25:44,580
At that moment, I was lost.
I didn't know what to do.

531
00:25:44,910 --> 00:25:46,380
My five o'clock looked solid.

532
00:25:47,050 --> 00:25:48,820
I was trying to free up the space
at my one o'clock.

533
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,180
So I wanted to keep at that.

534
00:25:50,180 --> 00:25:52,420
There was a small vehicle on my right.

535
00:25:52,550 --> 00:25:53,890
So I moved it to the left.

536
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:56,190
When I looked at it again,

537
00:25:56,460 --> 00:25:59,060
the triple-decker bus I had put there
had been gone.

538
00:26:01,630 --> 00:26:04,200
(The triple-decker bus
had been moved before his turn.)

539
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:06,900
By having the bus in the corner,
it strengthened our defense...

540
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:10,140
because the rear part
of the triple-decker bus was sticking out.

541
00:26:10,340 --> 00:26:12,570
That way, I could extract my car
while the other team couldn't...

542
00:26:12,570 --> 00:26:14,010
because of the bus.

543
00:26:15,170 --> 00:26:17,680
I set it up,
so that only we could extract ours.

544
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:21,080
Three people went before me
until it was my turn again.

545
00:26:21,410 --> 00:26:25,950
(The bus had been moved
while Jin Ho was away from the board.)

546
00:26:26,020 --> 00:26:27,390
I made a huge mistake.

547
00:26:27,490 --> 00:26:30,560
It would have taken the other team
at least 2 or 3 turns to extract the car.

548
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:33,960
But I let them skip the turns
and extract the car.

549
00:26:35,130 --> 00:26:36,560
I was super annoyed.

550
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:41,900
At that moment,
the car left the board in slow motion.

551
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:45,610
I was completely thrown off.
I didn't know what was going on.

552
00:26:49,210 --> 00:26:52,280
When he's flustered, he makes this face.

553
00:26:53,010 --> 00:26:56,350
I sensed it then
that he might have made a mistake.

554
00:27:03,460 --> 00:27:05,760
When you're focused too much
only on your own route,

555
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:08,090
there will come a moment
you become blind to other routes.

556
00:27:08,290 --> 00:27:09,960
Our team got one red car out.

557
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:12,430
As for the yellow cars,

558
00:27:12,430 --> 00:27:14,900
Team P3 will need at least 2 or 3 turns
to extract them.

559
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,400
That means our team can stop them
no matter what.

560
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:18,970
We had a fighting chance now.

561
00:27:19,110 --> 00:27:21,510
Just like our team messed up,
they could mess up too.

562
00:27:21,510 --> 00:27:23,410
- See? Jin Ho makes mistakes too.
- Exactly.

563
00:27:23,710 --> 00:27:27,110
When you make a huge mistake,
it demoralizes you.

564
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:29,720
I'm sure it's the same way
even with the mighty player, Jin Ho.

565
00:27:30,150 --> 00:27:31,820
The moment has completely shifted.

566
00:27:33,590 --> 00:27:36,260
Team P3, your time is up.
Please switch players.

567
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:40,690
Darn it. I'm sorry.

568
00:27:40,860 --> 00:27:42,400
- The one at the top...
- Did you do that on purpose?

569
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:43,860
- Or you just missed it?
- I missed it.

570
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:50,570
It looked like something had gone wrong.

571
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:54,410
For the first time,
I felt anxious at that moment.

572
00:27:59,110 --> 00:28:01,410
After looking at Team P2,

573
00:28:01,410 --> 00:28:03,980
I realized that
Jin Hyeong was making all the moves.

574
00:28:03,980 --> 00:28:06,520
It made me wonder
if that was more efficient.

575
00:28:06,550 --> 00:28:10,420
With our team, one player
could have done something for offense.

576
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:14,430
But another player might end up
wasting their turn to play defense.

577
00:28:14,590 --> 00:28:18,430
It made me think that Team P2's strategy
might be more efficient.

578
00:28:18,560 --> 00:28:20,770
Be calm. You can use up the whole minute.

579
00:28:21,230 --> 00:28:23,340
If we keep this up, we'll be able to...

580
00:28:23,340 --> 00:28:24,840
- keep the momentum going.
- I agree.

581
00:28:38,150 --> 00:28:39,690
It's Team P3's turn.

582
00:28:39,690 --> 00:28:40,720
(Seong Beom plays his move quickly.)

583
00:28:40,720 --> 00:28:42,190
It's Team P2's turn.

584
00:28:43,490 --> 00:28:45,260
If I lost my focus here,

585
00:28:45,260 --> 00:28:47,930
my entire team would end up going home.

586
00:28:48,190 --> 00:28:50,560
That actually helped me refocus.

587
00:28:50,860 --> 00:28:52,600
Our initial priority was
to block the red car...

588
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:55,170
which they ended up extracting.
It became clear I didn't have to do that.

589
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:57,670
I realized that I could focus on offense.

590
00:28:57,670 --> 00:29:01,410
After that, calculating my moves
suddenly became easy.

591
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:06,580
Whenever I played my moves fast,
they took longer time to think.

592
00:29:07,010 --> 00:29:08,950
I was able to...

593
00:29:08,950 --> 00:29:12,090
develop my strategy on my opponent's time.

594
00:29:14,450 --> 00:29:17,620
(While his opponent is thinking,)

595
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:20,730
(Seong Beom is thinking
about his next move.)

596
00:29:22,030 --> 00:29:25,160
After my opponent made his move,
I didn't have to think again.

597
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:29,270
I was able to keep making my moves
while barely spending my time.

598
00:29:29,840 --> 00:29:31,470
It allowed me to play...

599
00:29:31,470 --> 00:29:34,170
while utilizing their time as my own.

600
00:29:34,170 --> 00:29:35,610
I kept pursuing that strategy.

601
00:29:36,340 --> 00:29:37,680
That's when I thought...

602
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:41,080
I should lead this game.

603
00:29:43,580 --> 00:29:46,550
When it took us 1 minute to make 1 move,

604
00:29:46,550 --> 00:29:49,220
Seong Beom made 3 or 4 moves
within 10 seconds.

605
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:52,090
It felt like it was Seong Beom
versus the three of us.

606
00:29:53,030 --> 00:29:54,630
It's Team P3's turn.

607
00:29:54,630 --> 00:29:57,330
(Team P3's yellow car
is getting close to the exit.)

608
00:29:58,970 --> 00:30:00,430
It's Team P2's turn.

609
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:03,670
It's Team P3's turn.

610
00:30:09,310 --> 00:30:10,410
Your time is up.

611
00:30:11,980 --> 00:30:13,910
How many people
is Seong Beom going up against?

612
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:18,420
Seong Beom was able to focus on the game
as if he was possessed or something.

613
00:30:18,890 --> 00:30:21,850
He was up against Seung Jin,
YunB, and Jin Hyeong.

614
00:30:21,850 --> 00:30:23,960
While the other team took six turns,

615
00:30:24,120 --> 00:30:26,760
Seong Beom quickly made his moves nonstop.

616
00:30:27,590 --> 00:30:28,760
Your time is up.

617
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,330
(Lee Jin Hyeong of Team P2 switches
with YunB.)

618
00:30:33,570 --> 00:30:35,030
It's Team P2's turn.

619
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:58,320
You have 30 seconds left.

620
00:30:58,320 --> 00:31:02,730
(YunB)

621
00:31:10,500 --> 00:31:13,010
(YunB)

622
00:31:13,010 --> 00:31:14,340
You have ten seconds left.

623
00:31:18,240 --> 00:31:22,450
(Stopping)

624
00:31:22,650 --> 00:31:24,680
Team P2, your time is up.

625
00:31:26,190 --> 00:31:29,360
You didn't make a move.
It's Team P3's turn now.

626
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:40,500
Why didn't you make a move?

627
00:31:41,700 --> 00:31:42,700
Why didn't you play?

628
00:31:44,070 --> 00:31:46,310
- Why didn't you play?
- No talking.

629
00:31:46,310 --> 00:31:47,310
- We'll talk here.
- Okay.

630
00:31:47,970 --> 00:31:50,010
It doesn't matter
how well you play the games.

631
00:31:50,340 --> 00:31:53,050
The dumbest mistake is losing a turn.

632
00:31:53,150 --> 00:31:55,650
Every turn was so important.

633
00:31:56,920 --> 00:31:58,580
I was too focused.

634
00:31:58,950 --> 00:32:02,490
I wasn't aware that my minute had been up.

635
00:32:02,560 --> 00:32:04,660
I lost my turn to Seong Beom.

636
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:06,430
I was an idiot.

637
00:32:07,130 --> 00:32:08,130
Seriously.

638
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:13,470
Jin Hyeong was trying his best to deal
with his disappointment and frustration.

639
00:32:15,070 --> 00:32:16,870
First of all,
I feel so guilty toward Jin Hyeong.

640
00:32:19,710 --> 00:32:20,740
It's okay.

641
00:32:20,970 --> 00:32:23,110
Of course,
losing a turn is very disappointing.

642
00:32:23,210 --> 00:32:25,650
"It's your fault." "It's his fault."

643
00:32:26,280 --> 00:32:28,920
I didn't have time to place blame.
There was no reason to do that either.

644
00:32:29,050 --> 00:32:30,580
It had already happened.

645
00:32:30,580 --> 00:32:33,720
We only had to focus on what to do next.

646
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:36,460
Here's what you do when you're confused.
Look for a deadlock.

647
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:38,220
There are things you could add
even if they seem meaningless.

648
00:32:38,220 --> 00:32:39,930
For instance, let's say this is here.

649
00:32:40,030 --> 00:32:41,890
Moving this vehicle won't matter...

650
00:32:41,890 --> 00:32:43,900
since there will be three boxes left.
It's the same thing.

651
00:32:44,030 --> 00:32:45,560
- You could do that next time.
- Okay.

652
00:32:45,670 --> 00:32:48,070
Just like that.
Think about double parking.

653
00:32:48,530 --> 00:32:50,100
It's Team P3's turn.

654
00:32:50,100 --> 00:32:51,240
(It's Team P3's turn
as YunB failed to make a move.)

655
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:53,340
He made a mistake he should never make.

656
00:32:53,740 --> 00:32:55,010
They just wasted a turn.

657
00:32:55,010 --> 00:32:56,810
It means I could take two turns in a row.

658
00:32:59,910 --> 00:33:01,250
You have ten seconds left.

659
00:33:07,290 --> 00:33:08,820
It's Team P3's turn.

660
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:10,120
It's Team P2's turn.

661
00:33:10,420 --> 00:33:11,620
Your time is up.

662
00:33:11,860 --> 00:33:16,500
(Ha Seung Jin of Team P2 switches
with Lee Jin Hyeong.)

663
00:33:18,300 --> 00:33:21,670
The yellow car on my left
was getting close to the exit.

664
00:33:21,970 --> 00:33:24,070
I had the biggest chance of extracting...

665
00:33:24,070 --> 00:33:25,570
the yellow car on my top right
in my opinion.

666
00:33:26,410 --> 00:33:28,570
I wanted to play this right
and extract it.

667
00:33:30,310 --> 00:33:31,740
It's Team P3's turn.

668
00:33:31,740 --> 00:33:34,710
(Seong Beom starts targeting
the north side.)

669
00:33:36,020 --> 00:33:37,580
We wasted a turn.

670
00:33:37,580 --> 00:33:39,690
So the yellow car
was bound to make it out at some point.

671
00:33:39,690 --> 00:33:41,020
(It's impossible to block the yellow car.)

672
00:33:48,890 --> 00:33:50,230
Your time is up.

673
00:33:50,330 --> 00:33:52,260
(Heo Seong Beom of Team P3 switches
with Choi Hye Seon.)

674
00:33:57,770 --> 00:33:59,210
It's Team P3's turn.

675
00:34:01,070 --> 00:34:02,580
It's Team P2's turn.

676
00:34:06,650 --> 00:34:08,080
It's Team P3's turn.

677
00:34:08,080 --> 00:34:10,220
(Team P3 extracts their 1st car.)

678
00:34:10,350 --> 00:34:11,920
It was very painful to watch.

679
00:34:12,690 --> 00:34:14,950
Despite that,
I didn't have any reason to give up.

680
00:34:15,290 --> 00:34:17,520
(Choi Hye Seon of Team P3 switches
with Xitsuh.)

681
00:34:19,190 --> 00:34:20,990
I thought about which car to extract next.

682
00:34:21,490 --> 00:34:24,530
It was quite clear
for Team P3 and our team.

683
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:28,500
Clearly, Team P3 should try
to get the yellow car close to the exit.

684
00:34:28,970 --> 00:34:31,570
Our team had to extract
the red car on the bottom.

685
00:34:33,770 --> 00:34:35,910
(It's Hong Jin Ho's turn.)

686
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:40,310
Your time is up.

687
00:34:40,310 --> 00:34:43,550
(Hong Jin Ho of Team 3 switches
with Heo Seong Beom.)

688
00:34:45,890 --> 00:34:46,990
I didn't...

689
00:34:47,190 --> 00:34:49,460
make a lot of moves because it seemed
Seong Beom was onto something big.

690
00:34:49,620 --> 00:34:52,060
I became a bit timid
after making a mistake.

691
00:34:52,060 --> 00:34:54,590
So we decided to
let Seong Beom take the wheel.

692
00:34:55,490 --> 00:34:57,130
They're letting Seong Beom lead.

693
00:34:57,230 --> 00:34:58,230
Yes.

694
00:34:58,330 --> 00:34:59,700
It's Jin Hyeong versus Seong Beom.

695
00:35:08,310 --> 00:35:09,840
It's Team P3's turn.

696
00:35:10,380 --> 00:35:11,880
It's Team P2's turn.

697
00:35:15,450 --> 00:35:16,880
It's Team P3's turn.

698
00:35:20,620 --> 00:35:21,850
It's Team P2's turn.

699
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:25,120
It's Team P3's turn.

700
00:35:25,590 --> 00:35:27,130
It's Team P2's turn.

701
00:35:27,790 --> 00:35:31,230
It was like watching two generals
from different countries compete.

702
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:35,030
They radiated this aura, so intense that
it was impossible to even talk to them.

703
00:35:35,870 --> 00:35:37,770
I had to play fast
in situations like this.

704
00:35:37,970 --> 00:35:40,670
Forcing the pace to speed up...

705
00:35:40,770 --> 00:35:43,580
was bound to trigger strategic foresight.

706
00:35:43,580 --> 00:35:45,310
There was bound
to be one mistake at least.

707
00:35:56,190 --> 00:35:58,390
Their mental chess was insane.

708
00:35:58,390 --> 00:35:59,530
It was super cool.

709
00:36:05,330 --> 00:36:06,430
Your time is up.

710
00:36:10,500 --> 00:36:13,570
One of the most important rules
in Brutal Morning Commute is...

711
00:36:14,070 --> 00:36:16,140
Whenever you come up to the board,

712
00:36:16,140 --> 00:36:18,240
you have to redo your calculations.

713
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:21,680
When my opponent redid the calculations,
I could use the time for my strategy.

714
00:36:21,810 --> 00:36:24,450
The moment they made their move,
it was exactly what I had anticipated.

715
00:36:24,450 --> 00:36:26,790
That allowed me to make my move
within one second.

716
00:36:27,750 --> 00:36:30,390
After that point,
I was brimming with confidence.

717
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:32,460
"I can read his every move."

718
00:36:32,660 --> 00:36:33,990
"This is fun."

719
00:36:35,760 --> 00:36:36,830
I'm about to piss myself.

720
00:36:37,930 --> 00:36:41,370
I felt that I finally understood
this game perfectly.

721
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:43,100
How cunning.

722
00:36:43,270 --> 00:36:45,100
Seong Beom was good. He's smart.

723
00:36:45,840 --> 00:36:46,970
Since Seong Beom is leading the game,

724
00:36:46,970 --> 00:36:49,070
- we shouldn't mess it up.
- Right.

725
00:36:49,310 --> 00:36:51,180
I'll just move any piece.

726
00:36:51,180 --> 00:36:52,780
I'm just moving one at a time too.

727
00:36:52,780 --> 00:36:54,450
Team P2, your time is up.

728
00:36:57,420 --> 00:37:01,620
(Team P2 player is switched to YunB.)

729
00:37:01,950 --> 00:37:03,360
It's Team P2's turn.

730
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:11,360
(YunB)

731
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:14,630
- Did YunB make his move?
- He hasn't yet.

732
00:37:15,570 --> 00:37:17,200
It's not that I don't trust YunB,

733
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:20,540
but we must block the yellow car
in the north no matter what.

734
00:37:20,910 --> 00:37:21,910
So...

735
00:37:22,510 --> 00:37:25,210
I thought YunB would make a move
in the north.

736
00:37:25,740 --> 00:37:27,550
To do that,
he needed to stretch his left arm.

737
00:37:28,450 --> 00:37:30,550
But for some reason,

738
00:37:30,750 --> 00:37:32,990
his hand was clearly not there.

739
00:37:33,750 --> 00:37:37,390
His right hand was
about to do something in the south.

740
00:37:37,620 --> 00:37:38,620
Timeout.

741
00:37:38,620 --> 00:37:41,560
(Timeout)

742
00:37:41,560 --> 00:37:43,460
Team P2 has requested for a timeout.

743
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:44,830
I felt really bad,

744
00:37:45,460 --> 00:37:46,830
but I thought I should stop this first.

745
00:37:47,300 --> 00:37:48,930
"Let's hear out what he wants to do."

746
00:37:49,170 --> 00:37:50,770
What were you going to do?

747
00:37:51,300 --> 00:37:53,310
I want to move this to here.

748
00:37:53,310 --> 00:37:54,310
Why?

749
00:37:54,570 --> 00:37:55,870
I heard his explanation,

750
00:37:55,870 --> 00:37:57,510
and it wasn't completely groundless.

751
00:37:57,780 --> 00:38:00,150
They definitely were moves
that we'd need at some point.

752
00:38:00,150 --> 00:38:01,980
But what we needed at that moment...

753
00:38:02,310 --> 00:38:04,080
was to stop the yellow car on top...

754
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:06,320
from leaving its spot.

755
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:08,750
What do I need to attack first?

756
00:38:09,290 --> 00:38:11,660
I think...
You haven't made your move yet, right?

757
00:38:11,660 --> 00:38:13,290
- Pull that down first.
- That one?

758
00:38:13,290 --> 00:38:14,290
Pull that down,

759
00:38:14,560 --> 00:38:16,300
and Seong Beom will move this piece.

760
00:38:16,300 --> 00:38:18,400
- He needs to block this from moving.
- This first.

761
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:20,670
Leave that piece there.

762
00:38:21,230 --> 00:38:23,240
For Seung Jin,
move that to the right, and that's done.

763
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:25,340
- Which one?
- The one above the barricade.

764
00:38:25,340 --> 00:38:27,170
- What?
- The one right above the barricade.

765
00:38:27,170 --> 00:38:28,710
- Push it to this side?
- To the right up.

766
00:38:28,710 --> 00:38:30,280
I was going to move this.

767
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:32,680
I'll move the small one up.

768
00:38:32,680 --> 00:38:34,150
Move it up,

769
00:38:34,150 --> 00:38:37,220
and move this small one here.
They'll need many moves to block it.

770
00:38:37,220 --> 00:38:39,720
We need to move them...

771
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:42,550
to move the long ones to the sides
and make way for this car.

772
00:38:42,550 --> 00:38:45,390
So this is our best move.

773
00:38:45,390 --> 00:38:48,560
The opponent was coming up with
a strategy to open up the lower left,

774
00:38:48,790 --> 00:38:51,060
so our priority was to defend that side.

775
00:38:51,060 --> 00:38:52,200
Secondly,

776
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:53,700
with the yellow car,
which could move to the north,

777
00:38:53,700 --> 00:38:56,240
I made some moves
as if I'd move it to the other side.

778
00:38:56,240 --> 00:38:58,170
I tried to trick them that way too.

779
00:38:58,170 --> 00:38:59,770
The timeout is over.

780
00:38:59,770 --> 00:39:02,210
Please go back to your seats.

781
00:39:03,010 --> 00:39:05,080
Team P2 will start the turn.

782
00:39:06,050 --> 00:39:07,150
(Two of them make moves as they planned.)

783
00:39:07,150 --> 00:39:08,880
It's Team P3's turn.

784
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,250
It's Team P2's turn.

785
00:39:11,450 --> 00:39:12,690
Your time is up.

786
00:39:14,490 --> 00:39:17,990
(YunB of Team P2 switches
with Ha Seung Jin.)

787
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:19,360
It's Team P2's turn.

788
00:39:20,630 --> 00:39:24,830
(Seung Jin makes the move
as per Jin Hyeong's instructions.)

789
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:27,070
It's Team P3's turn.

790
00:39:28,200 --> 00:39:29,570
It's Team P2's turn.

791
00:39:30,370 --> 00:39:33,110
We don't have any timeout left,

792
00:39:33,110 --> 00:39:36,140
so I should just make one move per turn,

793
00:39:36,140 --> 00:39:37,710
and I should leave all the big moves...

794
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:40,050
to Jin Hyeong.

795
00:39:40,550 --> 00:39:41,750
Your time is up.

796
00:39:44,250 --> 00:39:47,690
In the end, it's all about
how few mistakes...

797
00:39:47,690 --> 00:39:51,090
the other teammates make in the battle...

798
00:39:51,090 --> 00:39:53,260
of Lee Jin Hyeong and Heo Seong Beom,

799
00:39:53,260 --> 00:39:55,030
and how well we support them.

800
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:59,730
(Choi Hye Seon of Team P3 switches
with Xitsuh.)

801
00:40:00,970 --> 00:40:02,400
It's Team P3's turn.

802
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:05,700
I stood in front of the board
against Jin Hyeong when it was my turn.

803
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:11,140
If I moved the bus on top,

804
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:15,980
in two turns,
the yellow car could move out.

805
00:40:16,620 --> 00:40:18,750
So I thought it was a really good chance.

806
00:40:18,980 --> 00:40:20,350
I pretended to think hard.

807
00:40:21,020 --> 00:40:22,390
Please pull out.

808
00:40:22,390 --> 00:40:24,320
I made the move, acting like I moved it...

809
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:26,260
because there was nothing else to move.

810
00:40:26,860 --> 00:40:28,290
It's Team P2's turn.

811
00:40:31,500 --> 00:40:32,500
I made...

812
00:40:33,130 --> 00:40:34,600
a big mistake.

813
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:38,270
Pull out the bus.

814
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:41,270
It's not over until it is.

815
00:40:42,070 --> 00:40:44,580
No matter how far the victory seems,

816
00:40:44,580 --> 00:40:46,280
if you run hard enough, you can grab it.

817
00:40:47,480 --> 00:40:51,320
There was no way to stop
the red car from moving out.

818
00:40:54,020 --> 00:40:58,220
The car which was moved last
was there of all places,

819
00:40:58,220 --> 00:41:02,190
so I couldn't stop the red car
from moving out.

820
00:41:02,190 --> 00:41:04,030
(Xitsuh cannot block the red car's path.)

821
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:06,000
You have ten seconds left.

822
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:09,200
But I thought really hard
in that situation.

823
00:41:09,540 --> 00:41:11,570
"Should we score one each?"

824
00:41:11,570 --> 00:41:15,610
"Or is there a better way?"

825
00:41:15,610 --> 00:41:16,880
Your time is up.

826
00:41:17,540 --> 00:41:18,980
Then my time was up.

827
00:41:20,980 --> 00:41:22,780
- I think we need a timeout.
- What?

828
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:24,280
Are we in a tight spot?

829
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:26,350
- I think we need a timeout.
- Really?

830
00:41:26,850 --> 00:41:29,420
As Xitsuh came back, he looked dejected.

831
00:41:29,420 --> 00:41:30,990
He said, "I think we need a timeout."

832
00:41:31,460 --> 00:41:32,760
Just say timeout.

833
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:34,060
We'd like a timeout.

834
00:41:34,060 --> 00:41:35,560
Team P3 has requested for a timeout,

835
00:41:35,560 --> 00:41:37,660
so you'll have
a five-minute strategy meeting.

836
00:41:37,660 --> 00:41:38,730
(Team P3's timeout)

837
00:41:39,060 --> 00:41:41,000
I can't stop the red car from moving out.

838
00:41:41,600 --> 00:41:42,600
You can't?

839
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:44,240
We can't block it here. You get it, right?

840
00:41:44,240 --> 00:41:45,400
- I got it.
- The cone is here,

841
00:41:45,400 --> 00:41:46,470
- and it was here.
- Okay.

842
00:41:46,470 --> 00:41:48,340
- I moved 1, and he moved 1.
- It's okay.

843
00:41:48,340 --> 00:41:50,080
- And we came to this.
- I understand.

844
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,710
I checked the board,

845
00:41:51,710 --> 00:41:53,510
and I understood what Xitsuh meant.

846
00:41:54,380 --> 00:41:56,850
When did they breach the left defense
so badly?

847
00:41:57,320 --> 00:41:59,520
I thought we had the upper hand,

848
00:41:59,990 --> 00:42:01,320
but how did it turn out like this?

849
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:04,460
We should get ourselves together...

850
00:42:04,660 --> 00:42:05,820
and win this.

851
00:42:06,830 --> 00:42:09,230
- No, it's okay.
- It's our turn.

852
00:42:09,230 --> 00:42:11,360
- Look.
- This...

853
00:42:11,360 --> 00:42:12,360
That...

854
00:42:13,170 --> 00:42:14,600
If he tries to move that,

855
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:15,930
we should move out ours too.

856
00:42:15,930 --> 00:42:16,940
If they try to block it,

857
00:42:16,940 --> 00:42:18,700
we can breach their bottom line.

858
00:42:18,700 --> 00:42:20,570
So just let them move out theirs,
and we should move our yellow car out too.

859
00:42:20,570 --> 00:42:21,870
- There's no other choice.
- So you mean...

860
00:42:21,870 --> 00:42:23,240
we should just score one each.

861
00:42:23,240 --> 00:42:24,240
Yes. First...

862
00:42:24,240 --> 00:42:26,280
I told him
to move out the car on the right.

863
00:42:26,980 --> 00:42:29,180
We needed to remove another yellow car
after that,

864
00:42:29,180 --> 00:42:31,820
so we focused on planning
for the next steps.

865
00:42:31,820 --> 00:42:34,090
In the end, we need to watch carefully
whether to move the yellow car...

866
00:42:34,090 --> 00:42:35,720
to the top or to the bottom.

867
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:38,520
I think moving it to the top is easier.

868
00:42:38,520 --> 00:42:40,530
Even if we can't move it out at once,

869
00:42:40,530 --> 00:42:42,460
move it all the way to the end,
leaving just one square.

870
00:42:42,460 --> 00:42:44,500
Put it right in front of that bus,
and we secure the win.

871
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:45,500
It's a checkmate.

872
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:48,930
"As long as it moves to where the bus is,"

873
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,470
"it's a checkmate."

874
00:42:50,900 --> 00:42:52,400
The game would be over...

875
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:54,510
once we moved it next to the bus.

876
00:42:54,510 --> 00:42:57,140
Our goal was never to move this car...

877
00:42:57,140 --> 00:42:58,810
until we were ready.

878
00:42:59,240 --> 00:43:00,650
The timeout is over.

879
00:43:00,650 --> 00:43:02,250
Please go back to your seats.

880
00:43:07,290 --> 00:43:10,290
In the end, Team P3 will move out
the yellow car to the top,

881
00:43:10,290 --> 00:43:12,060
and we'll move the red car out
to the left.

882
00:43:12,060 --> 00:43:14,630
The yellow car can move out in two turns,

883
00:43:14,630 --> 00:43:16,360
and we can move the red car out
in one turn.

884
00:43:16,660 --> 00:43:18,660
In the end, we saved one turn.

885
00:43:18,660 --> 00:43:21,230
Every single turn is precious now.

886
00:43:21,230 --> 00:43:23,170
They'll move the red car out,

887
00:43:23,170 --> 00:43:24,440
but once we move out the yellow car,

888
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:26,370
it's two-all.

889
00:43:26,670 --> 00:43:29,940
The decisive move for the final car...

890
00:43:29,940 --> 00:43:31,640
is blocked by us,

891
00:43:31,640 --> 00:43:32,950
so we can make the call.

892
00:43:33,180 --> 00:43:35,480
Team P3 will start the turn.

893
00:43:37,850 --> 00:43:40,990
(As they planned, Jin Ho opens up
the exit to the north.)

894
00:43:40,990 --> 00:43:42,350
It's Team P2's turn.

895
00:43:44,020 --> 00:43:45,390
It's Team P3's turn.

896
00:43:46,160 --> 00:43:48,360
(Jin Ho is ready
to move out the yellow car too.)

897
00:43:48,360 --> 00:43:49,860
It's Team P2's turn.

898
00:43:50,130 --> 00:43:51,560
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

899
00:43:51,830 --> 00:43:54,830
(Team P2's 2nd car moves out.)

900
00:43:54,830 --> 00:43:56,230
It's Team P3's turn.

901
00:43:57,670 --> 00:43:59,000
You have ten seconds left.

902
00:44:02,370 --> 00:44:04,110
(Team P3's 2nd car moves out.)

903
00:44:04,110 --> 00:44:05,510
It's Team P2's turn.

904
00:44:06,140 --> 00:44:07,650
Our team's car has moved out,

905
00:44:07,650 --> 00:44:09,150
and their car has moved out too.

906
00:44:09,750 --> 00:44:11,680
We're only left with the last car.

907
00:44:11,880 --> 00:44:14,390
We get to make the first move...

908
00:44:14,690 --> 00:44:16,390
because we'd trapped their car.

909
00:44:16,660 --> 00:44:18,720
Before we pull out our car,

910
00:44:19,220 --> 00:44:20,530
the red car can't move.

911
00:44:21,260 --> 00:44:23,060
The only thing we can hope for...

912
00:44:23,060 --> 00:44:25,030
is for the opponent to make a mistake.

913
00:44:25,330 --> 00:44:26,770
It's not likely.

914
00:44:27,070 --> 00:44:29,100
But there's no reason to give up.

915
00:44:29,100 --> 00:44:30,600
You have 30 seconds left.

916
00:44:33,910 --> 00:44:35,310
It's Team P3's turn.

917
00:44:37,040 --> 00:44:38,280
Your time is up.

918
00:44:38,280 --> 00:44:40,250
(Hong Jin Ho of Team P3 switches
with Heo Seong Beom.)

919
00:44:45,320 --> 00:44:46,650
It's Team P3's turn.

920
00:44:47,990 --> 00:44:49,590
(Seong Beom starts
to clear the western path.)

921
00:44:49,590 --> 00:44:50,990
It's Team P2's turn.

922
00:44:53,960 --> 00:44:55,290
Your time is up.

923
00:45:05,970 --> 00:45:07,340
It's Team P2's turn.

924
00:45:08,670 --> 00:45:11,180
Which car should we move out and to where?

925
00:45:11,440 --> 00:45:12,580
Based on how it's being played out,

926
00:45:13,410 --> 00:45:15,080
we don't have the upper hand,
to be honest.

927
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:18,650
The yellow car only needs two turns
to move to the left.

928
00:45:19,580 --> 00:45:22,820
But both red cars's paths to the top
are blocked by the yellow car.

929
00:45:23,560 --> 00:45:24,990
Then the pieces we can move,

930
00:45:24,990 --> 00:45:27,730
the pieces we should try to move.

931
00:45:27,860 --> 00:45:29,900
The only place we could aim for
was the lower right.

932
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:35,000
That area is full of cars.

933
00:45:35,130 --> 00:45:39,140
A bunch of cars all tangled up
on a highway,

934
00:45:39,140 --> 00:45:40,440
some trying to nose in,

935
00:45:40,440 --> 00:45:42,840
and some stuck there and honking.
That's what's happening.

936
00:45:43,180 --> 00:45:44,440
And there's only one way...

937
00:45:44,440 --> 00:45:46,750
for us to turn the tables.

938
00:45:47,010 --> 00:45:50,650
The opponent has to make 2 or 3 mistakes.

939
00:45:51,020 --> 00:45:52,580
With that one hope in mind,

940
00:45:52,580 --> 00:45:53,690
I waited for the next turn.

941
00:45:54,090 --> 00:45:55,590
It's Team P3's turn.

942
00:45:56,290 --> 00:45:57,360
(Seong Beom clears the obstacles
in the west one by one.)

943
00:45:57,360 --> 00:45:58,520
It's Team P2's turn.

944
00:45:59,620 --> 00:46:03,860
I was determined to become
even more focused then.

945
00:46:03,900 --> 00:46:06,800
Usually, in this kind of situation,
the opponents make mistakes in excitement,

946
00:46:06,800 --> 00:46:09,030
and we make mistakes too,
so let's not do that.

947
00:46:09,430 --> 00:46:11,240
Let's stay calm until the end...

948
00:46:11,240 --> 00:46:12,500
and secure a perfect victory.

949
00:46:12,870 --> 00:46:14,040
That was what I thought.

950
00:46:14,240 --> 00:46:15,710
It's Team P3's turn.

951
00:46:18,340 --> 00:46:20,110
(Seong Beom persistently aims
for the west.)

952
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:21,610
It's Team P2's turn.

953
00:46:22,250 --> 00:46:23,480
Your time is up.

954
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:29,790
But just like Zhang Fei...

955
00:46:29,790 --> 00:46:31,390
in the Battle of Changban,

956
00:46:31,890 --> 00:46:33,020
Seong Beom didn't budge.

957
00:46:34,230 --> 00:46:35,460
Your time is up.

958
00:46:36,860 --> 00:46:38,030
Your time is up.

959
00:46:38,030 --> 00:46:39,030
(Seong Beom keeps his turn
by making fast moves.)

960
00:46:39,030 --> 00:46:40,270
Your time is up.

961
00:46:41,900 --> 00:46:43,370
Team P2, your time is up.

962
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:46,970
YunB came back before him,

963
00:46:46,970 --> 00:46:48,210
and so did Seung Jin.

964
00:46:48,310 --> 00:46:49,370
I went up next.

965
00:46:49,940 --> 00:46:51,040
The moment I saw the board,

966
00:46:51,980 --> 00:46:54,380
I got the confirmation.

967
00:46:54,650 --> 00:46:57,950
(The path to the west
is completely opened up.)

968
00:47:04,320 --> 00:47:05,920
Even if we dragged this on,

969
00:47:05,960 --> 00:47:08,830
we'd lose out in terms of
the number of turns needed anyway,

970
00:47:09,800 --> 00:47:11,100
and since the opponent was Seong Beom,

971
00:47:11,100 --> 00:47:13,270
he wouldn't make a mistake.

972
00:47:16,700 --> 00:47:18,470
As time went by,

973
00:47:19,070 --> 00:47:21,770
Jin Hyeong didn't seem like
he was losing focus,

974
00:47:22,170 --> 00:47:24,940
but his face...

975
00:47:24,940 --> 00:47:26,440
started to lose its color.

976
00:47:27,450 --> 00:47:29,250
That moment comes at one point.

977
00:47:29,250 --> 00:47:30,520
I did my best,

978
00:47:30,880 --> 00:47:33,150
and I worked really hard. Despite that,

979
00:47:33,720 --> 00:47:36,590
there's a moment when you can clearly see
the winner has been decided.

980
00:47:37,920 --> 00:47:39,460
That was the moment.

981
00:47:42,430 --> 00:47:43,530
I judged...

982
00:47:44,060 --> 00:47:46,530
that there was 0 possibility
of our 2 red cars...

983
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:49,900
moving out before the two yellow cars did.

984
00:47:58,210 --> 00:47:59,710
It's Team P3's turn.

985
00:48:01,650 --> 00:48:02,880
It's Team P2's turn.

986
00:48:02,880 --> 00:48:05,080
- Checkmate.
- Yes. Good job.

987
00:48:21,130 --> 00:48:22,530
It's Team P3's turn.

988
00:48:24,670 --> 00:48:25,940
It's Team P2's turn.

989
00:48:30,410 --> 00:48:31,680
It's Team P3's turn.

990
00:48:32,910 --> 00:48:33,910
I'm moving it out.

991
00:48:33,910 --> 00:48:36,350
(Team P3's 3rd car is moved out.)

992
00:48:36,350 --> 00:48:37,380
Congratulations.

993
00:48:41,920 --> 00:48:44,920
I'm sorry for getting on edge.

994
00:48:45,760 --> 00:48:46,930
I'm sorry.

995
00:48:50,700 --> 00:48:51,860
You should've improved your image better.

996
00:48:52,430 --> 00:48:53,570
Improve what?

997
00:48:53,830 --> 00:48:55,100
Good job.

998
00:48:55,100 --> 00:48:56,100
Good job, Seung Jin.

999
00:48:56,770 --> 00:48:58,300
- You worked hard.
- Good job.

1000
00:48:58,300 --> 00:49:01,010
- You did so well.
- Good job.

1001
00:49:03,110 --> 00:49:05,510
I did my best, YunB did his best,

1002
00:49:05,510 --> 00:49:06,710
and Seung Jin did his best.

1003
00:49:06,710 --> 00:49:08,150
We all did our best.

1004
00:49:08,510 --> 00:49:09,850
Who made what mistake?

1005
00:49:10,320 --> 00:49:11,880
Who should be responsible for what?

1006
00:49:11,880 --> 00:49:14,220
All these questions mean nothing to me.

1007
00:49:17,260 --> 00:49:18,760
The only thing that holds meaning to me...

1008
00:49:18,790 --> 00:49:21,030
is that we did our best,
and that it's a shame,

1009
00:49:21,430 --> 00:49:23,300
but the game has ended here.

1010
00:49:24,560 --> 00:49:27,070
(Today's Deathmatch has ended.)

1011
00:49:27,070 --> 00:49:29,200
The Deathmatch has ended.

1012
00:49:29,630 --> 00:49:32,370
Please gather in the main hall.

1013
00:49:37,440 --> 00:49:40,010
I will announce the result
of the Deathmatch.

1014
00:49:40,680 --> 00:49:43,250
The team which has been eliminated
from Bloody Game X is...

1015
00:49:45,150 --> 00:49:46,750
Team P2.

1016
00:49:50,890 --> 00:49:53,630
Team P2, please pack up right now...

1017
00:49:53,660 --> 00:49:55,630
and leave the Bloody Mansion.

1018
00:49:55,630 --> 00:49:57,800
- You worked so hard.
- Good job.

1019
00:49:57,800 --> 00:49:59,930
- You worked so hard, Seung Jin.
- Good job.

1020
00:49:59,930 --> 00:50:00,930
See you again.

1021
00:50:00,970 --> 00:50:02,570
Actually, I feel bad...

1022
00:50:03,030 --> 00:50:06,600
for the younger teammates.
I felt very sorry.

1023
00:50:06,740 --> 00:50:08,840
My favorite moment...

1024
00:50:09,310 --> 00:50:13,040
in this game is... It might be unexpected.

1025
00:50:14,310 --> 00:50:17,720
But it was when I undid the blind
and the gag while tied up...

1026
00:50:18,120 --> 00:50:20,220
and checked the faces next to me.

1027
00:50:20,720 --> 00:50:24,290
I saw Sung Joo, YunB, and Jin Hyeong.

1028
00:50:24,920 --> 00:50:28,690
And when I heard the announcement
that we were one team,

1029
00:50:29,530 --> 00:50:31,230
I felt the happiest.

1030
00:50:32,160 --> 00:50:33,800
In this place,
which is like walking on thin ice,

1031
00:50:34,330 --> 00:50:37,870
I have my teammates
whom I can trust and rely on.

1032
00:50:39,270 --> 00:50:40,770
I was very happy.

1033
00:50:41,610 --> 00:50:43,210
- Come here.
- My gosh.

1034
00:50:44,210 --> 00:50:47,010
- I should get back to society.
- Hey.

1035
00:50:49,080 --> 00:50:53,120
Team P2 being the 1st team
to get eliminated...

1036
00:50:53,120 --> 00:50:54,250
is such a shame.

1037
00:50:54,850 --> 00:50:56,250
If I'm to blame anyone,

1038
00:50:56,650 --> 00:50:58,520
I think I'm the most to blame.

1039
00:50:58,520 --> 00:51:00,790
I think the ACRO snowballed.

1040
00:51:00,790 --> 00:51:04,760
I'm ashamed to say I'm an experienced...

1041
00:51:04,900 --> 00:51:06,360
survival show participant.

1042
00:51:06,630 --> 00:51:08,030
Despite that,

1043
00:51:08,770 --> 00:51:12,340
I was glad
Team P2 could get together again.

1044
00:51:12,340 --> 00:51:14,770
Especially Jin Hyeong. Jin Hyeong...

1045
00:51:15,110 --> 00:51:17,180
The kid has changed.

1046
00:51:17,340 --> 00:51:20,310
He became really cool and mature.

1047
00:51:20,610 --> 00:51:22,110
I feel so bad for Jin Hyeong.

1048
00:51:22,410 --> 00:51:24,320
I feel bad for Seung Jin too.

1049
00:51:24,750 --> 00:51:26,790
Rather, I want to say this to Sung Joo.

1050
00:51:26,920 --> 00:51:30,020
Sung Joo, good for you
that you escaped Team P2.

1051
00:51:36,560 --> 00:51:37,730
Are you really leaving?

1052
00:51:37,730 --> 00:51:38,900
Yes, I'm really leaving.

1053
00:51:39,860 --> 00:51:41,300
See you back in the society.

1054
00:51:44,970 --> 00:51:46,440
- Jin Hyeong.
- Good job.

1055
00:51:46,440 --> 00:51:47,910
I'll carry on your will.

1056
00:51:47,910 --> 00:51:48,970
Good luck.

1057
00:51:49,310 --> 00:51:52,140
He must've had a hard time mentally.

1058
00:51:52,380 --> 00:51:55,310
The Jin Hyeong I saw
in the second season...

1059
00:51:55,310 --> 00:51:59,380
and the Jin Hyeong I saw in this season
were different.

1060
00:51:59,380 --> 00:52:02,320
Above all,
the position he held in his team...

1061
00:52:02,490 --> 00:52:04,260
gave him a lot of pressure.

1062
00:52:04,260 --> 00:52:06,090
In the end,

1063
00:52:06,090 --> 00:52:08,330
he made a self-destructive move.

1064
00:52:08,590 --> 00:52:10,800
When I saw that, I felt...

1065
00:52:11,030 --> 00:52:13,400
Seeing such a young guy
breaking down like that...

1066
00:52:13,730 --> 00:52:17,300
made me feel bitter.
And at the same time...

1067
00:52:17,540 --> 00:52:19,470
"We're definitely going to cry today."

1068
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:21,070
That was what I thought.

1069
00:52:22,140 --> 00:52:23,410
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

1070
00:52:23,580 --> 00:52:24,710
See you.

1071
00:52:24,710 --> 00:52:26,880
- Good luck.
- Good job.

1072
00:52:27,050 --> 00:52:28,210
You can do it.

1073
00:52:28,610 --> 00:52:29,880
Good job. Have a safe trip back.

1074
00:52:30,680 --> 00:52:32,520
- Good job, Seung Jin.
- Jin Hyeong, you worked so hard.

1075
00:52:32,520 --> 00:52:33,820
I really worked hard.

1076
00:52:33,820 --> 00:52:35,650
- Good job.
- You really worked hard.

1077
00:52:35,650 --> 00:52:37,820
- We played well as a team until the end.
- Yes.

1078
00:52:37,820 --> 00:52:39,220
We stayed loyal.

1079
00:52:43,560 --> 00:52:45,930
This is my first time getting eliminated.

1080
00:52:46,130 --> 00:52:48,500
I did wonder how it would feel.

1081
00:52:49,870 --> 00:52:51,440
But it feels a lot sadder than I thought.

1082
00:52:54,510 --> 00:52:57,640
I think I'm very unsociable,

1083
00:52:57,680 --> 00:52:59,410
tend to get ahead of myself,

1084
00:52:59,510 --> 00:53:02,250
so I get hate from a lot of people.

1085
00:53:02,650 --> 00:53:04,850
And I lack in many ways.

1086
00:53:05,120 --> 00:53:07,990
I think those are the reasons
why I played poorly...

1087
00:53:07,990 --> 00:53:10,560
in team games and main games.

1088
00:53:10,560 --> 00:53:12,760
Despite that, the reason...

1089
00:53:12,760 --> 00:53:15,030
I keep coming back to Bloody Game
and try it out...

1090
00:53:15,960 --> 00:53:17,030
I have one reason.

1091
00:53:17,030 --> 00:53:20,000
I really enjoy and love Bloody Game.

1092
00:53:32,340 --> 00:53:34,610
When Bloody Game 1 came out, it was 2021.

1093
00:53:34,850 --> 00:53:37,920
I went through a lot during that time.

1094
00:53:39,180 --> 00:53:40,190
So...

1095
00:53:40,820 --> 00:53:42,290
you know,

1096
00:53:42,290 --> 00:53:44,990
when you go through a very difficult time,

1097
00:53:45,520 --> 00:53:47,290
you don't remember most of the things
that have happened.

1098
00:53:47,290 --> 00:53:49,560
I don't even remember what I did
for my birthday that year.

1099
00:53:50,430 --> 00:53:51,460
But...

1100
00:53:52,830 --> 00:53:54,270
the only thing I can remember...

1101
00:53:54,270 --> 00:53:56,800
is that I really enjoyed
watching the first season of the show.

1102
00:54:00,170 --> 00:54:01,240
I'm sorry.

1103
00:54:03,580 --> 00:54:06,540
When they invited me for Season Two,
I accepted it gladly.

1104
00:54:06,780 --> 00:54:09,550
So I got too eager that I overdid it...

1105
00:54:10,250 --> 00:54:12,320
and got on a lot of people's bad sides.

1106
00:54:12,450 --> 00:54:14,420
I have absolutely no regrets about it.

1107
00:54:14,750 --> 00:54:17,490
So I really wanted to do well
in this season as well.

1108
00:54:17,990 --> 00:54:21,590
My teammates and I had fun
playing the games,

1109
00:54:21,830 --> 00:54:23,560
and we did our best.

1110
00:54:23,560 --> 00:54:24,860
But one thing...

1111
00:54:27,600 --> 00:54:28,600
is...

1112
00:54:29,900 --> 00:54:32,500
it's such a shame
that I wouldn't be part of...

1113
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:35,010
all the fun games and all the things...

1114
00:54:35,210 --> 00:54:38,780
that would happen in the Bloody Mansion
moving forward.

1115
00:54:39,240 --> 00:54:41,450
I'll leave with the memories.

1116
00:54:43,510 --> 00:54:44,550
I had fun.

1117
00:54:45,550 --> 00:54:46,750
Thank you.

1118
00:54:48,320 --> 00:54:49,750
- I had fun.
- It was fun.

1119
00:54:49,750 --> 00:54:50,820
I had fun.

1120
00:54:50,820 --> 00:54:52,620
I'm so sorry, Jin Hyeong.

1121
00:54:52,620 --> 00:54:54,330
- No, don't say that.
- Thank you.

1122
00:54:54,390 --> 00:54:57,130
I'll be reminded of this
every time I go to Seongsu-dong.

1123
00:54:57,130 --> 00:54:58,200
ACRO Seoul Forest.

1124
00:54:58,860 --> 00:55:00,100
Me too.

1125
00:55:02,930 --> 00:55:05,000
It feels empty with one whole team gone.

1126
00:55:05,170 --> 00:55:06,870
I know, right. It feels strange.

1127
00:55:06,870 --> 00:55:08,640
- Yes. Nobody sits here anymore.
- Right?

1128
00:55:09,140 --> 00:55:11,980
The whole team was gone,

1129
00:55:12,010 --> 00:55:13,510
and it felt very empty.

1130
00:55:13,650 --> 00:55:16,210
I felt really bad for Team P2,

1131
00:55:16,310 --> 00:55:17,950
but we had to go outdoors,

1132
00:55:18,250 --> 00:55:20,180
so I should use the time...

1133
00:55:20,180 --> 00:55:23,490
to worry about our survival
than worry about Team T2.

1134
00:55:25,460 --> 00:55:26,990
That could've been my fate.

1135
00:55:27,690 --> 00:55:28,730
This is scary.

1136
00:55:29,830 --> 00:55:31,530
It feels like
I've avoided the bullet like this.

1137
00:55:31,530 --> 00:55:33,630
- You're right.
- That's how we'll play.

1138
00:55:34,200 --> 00:55:37,540
Avoiding it narrowly? Keep avoiding it?

1139
00:55:38,370 --> 00:55:40,310
We already got grazed by a few shots.

1140
00:55:40,310 --> 00:55:42,310
Bleeding a bit is fine.

1141
00:55:42,410 --> 00:55:43,570
- We can just put some ointment.
- It's fine.

1142
00:55:43,570 --> 00:55:46,140
We just need to avoid getting shot
in the heart.

1143
00:55:46,140 --> 00:55:47,410
You're lucky, Sung Joo.

1144
00:55:47,950 --> 00:55:49,480
I saw the preview...

1145
00:55:49,480 --> 00:55:50,580
of my fate.

1146
00:55:50,680 --> 00:55:52,080
But I would've won if I had been
in that team.

1147
00:55:52,220 --> 00:55:53,380
Right, if you had been in that team.

1148
00:55:54,750 --> 00:55:56,090
Honestly, I don't think I could've won
against Team P3.

1149
00:55:56,320 --> 00:55:58,160
They're way too strong.

1150
00:56:02,190 --> 00:56:03,660
Here is an announcement.

1151
00:56:04,130 --> 00:56:05,730
Tomorrow's Money Challenge...

1152
00:56:07,930 --> 00:56:11,470
will be a 2-on-2 team alliance game.

1153
00:56:14,740 --> 00:56:17,880
Players, please form an alliance...

1154
00:56:17,940 --> 00:56:19,580
by mutual agreement.

1155
00:56:19,810 --> 00:56:20,880
Right away?

1156
00:56:20,880 --> 00:56:23,450
You can register the alliance team
in the Voting Room.

1157
00:56:23,750 --> 00:56:26,880
Two team representatives,
one from each team, must enter together.

1158
00:56:27,220 --> 00:56:28,850
Before registering the alliance team,

1159
00:56:28,850 --> 00:56:31,460
I will reveal tomorrow's Money Challenge.

1160
00:56:33,520 --> 00:56:35,290
Tomorrow's Money Challenge is...

1161
00:56:37,300 --> 00:56:38,400
(Equation Combo)

1162
00:56:38,400 --> 00:56:40,670
Equation Combo.

1163
00:56:43,330 --> 00:56:44,340
You.

1164
00:56:45,100 --> 00:56:46,200
It's my game.

1165
00:56:47,410 --> 00:56:48,940
They're good at it too.

1166
00:56:48,940 --> 00:56:49,970
All of them would be good at it.

1167
00:56:49,970 --> 00:56:53,580
Equation Combo is a game
which you must form an equation...

1168
00:56:53,580 --> 00:56:54,950
using the symbol and number tiles.

1169
00:56:55,580 --> 00:56:58,580
The game requires calculation skills
and stamina.

1170
00:56:58,580 --> 00:56:59,580
Stamina?

1171
00:56:59,780 --> 00:57:00,890
Equation Combo?

1172
00:57:01,750 --> 00:57:02,950
Everyone would agree...

1173
00:57:02,950 --> 00:57:05,760
that this game is the identity
of Bloody Game.

1174
00:57:05,760 --> 00:57:08,190
The game would require
both physical and mental aptitude.

1175
00:57:08,630 --> 00:57:10,930
I'm the best at calculations.

1176
00:57:10,930 --> 00:57:13,530
I thought I could play this game best.

1177
00:57:13,530 --> 00:57:15,070
We have Ji Hoo on our team.

1178
00:57:15,200 --> 00:57:16,200
He'd do well.

1179
00:57:16,300 --> 00:57:17,970
For stamina...

1180
00:57:18,170 --> 00:57:20,140
My team is pretty fit. We're fresh.

1181
00:57:20,570 --> 00:57:22,470
I'm preparing for a half marathon.

1182
00:57:22,470 --> 00:57:23,840
I play soccer twice a week.

1183
00:57:25,840 --> 00:57:26,840
What will you do?

1184
00:57:27,040 --> 00:57:30,110
None of us were physically strong
on my team.

1185
00:57:30,250 --> 00:57:33,120
Which team could supplement
our lack of strength...

1186
00:57:33,280 --> 00:57:36,350
and is good at the equation game
at the same time?

1187
00:57:36,350 --> 00:57:38,120
I thought Team C was it.

1188
00:57:39,790 --> 00:57:42,060
Those good at equations...

1189
00:57:42,530 --> 00:57:43,960
are 3 out of 4 teams.

1190
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:45,700
Everyone except Team Rookie is good.

1191
00:57:45,700 --> 00:57:46,760
Yes, so three teams.

1192
00:57:46,900 --> 00:57:50,470
Which team do you want to work with?
Tell me what you think, not as a team.

1193
00:57:50,740 --> 00:57:53,170
Personally, I want to play with you.

1194
00:57:53,340 --> 00:57:56,410
Personally, I also want to play with you.

1195
00:57:57,010 --> 00:58:00,140
You, Xitsuh, and him.

1196
00:58:00,450 --> 00:58:03,210
And I'll be helping you guys out.

1197
00:58:03,210 --> 00:58:05,820
- Then we could play the game really well.
- But...

1198
00:58:05,880 --> 00:58:07,490
We shouldn't think about the Deathmatch,

1199
00:58:07,490 --> 00:58:09,850
- but if things go wrong...
- I'm thinking that too.

1200
00:58:09,850 --> 00:58:12,020
If the Deathmatch were to happen
between the allied teams,

1201
00:58:12,920 --> 00:58:15,360
- it wouldn't look good for both of us.
- That's right.

1202
00:58:15,360 --> 00:58:16,560
That's what I'm thinking too.

1203
00:58:16,560 --> 00:58:18,800
We'd like to team up, but...

1204
00:58:18,900 --> 00:58:21,500
there's such a high chance
that the losing alliance team...

1205
00:58:21,500 --> 00:58:23,470
would go against each other
at the Deathmatch.

1206
00:58:23,500 --> 00:58:26,100
Us going against each other
wouldn't look too good.

1207
00:58:26,140 --> 00:58:28,210
I guess we both thought...

1208
00:58:28,210 --> 00:58:29,870
the other team was pretty strong.

1209
00:58:30,010 --> 00:58:31,640
What will we do?

1210
00:58:31,680 --> 00:58:32,780
Ji Hoo, come here.

1211
00:58:34,450 --> 00:58:35,950
- Hurry up.
- Okay.

1212
00:58:36,280 --> 00:58:38,780
- I want to team up with Team Rookie.
- Me too.

1213
00:58:38,780 --> 00:58:40,590
Seong Beom said the exact same thing.

1214
00:58:40,590 --> 00:58:42,320
- He wanted to form an alliance with us.
- Yes.

1215
00:58:42,420 --> 00:58:44,620
The only thing we're both worried about...

1216
00:58:44,620 --> 00:58:45,690
is that if we lose...

1217
00:58:45,690 --> 00:58:47,360
Deathmatch...
It'll be against the allied team.

1218
00:58:47,360 --> 00:58:48,830
- Us against them.
- You're right.

1219
00:58:48,990 --> 00:58:50,530
I think so too. Let's team up with Team R.

1220
00:58:50,530 --> 00:58:51,630
- Sure.
- That's why.

1221
00:58:51,630 --> 00:58:52,860
Yes, we thought that too.

1222
00:58:52,860 --> 00:58:55,170
I'll talk to Seong Beom about this.

1223
00:58:55,170 --> 00:58:56,170
Okay.

1224
00:58:56,430 --> 00:58:58,040
Since Team P3 is the strongest,

1225
00:58:58,470 --> 00:59:00,770
I thought we'd have the upper hand...

1226
00:59:00,770 --> 00:59:02,140
if two strong teams joined hands.

1227
00:59:02,140 --> 00:59:03,210
But if we end up in the Deathmatch,

1228
00:59:03,210 --> 00:59:04,880
there's a high chance
we'll go against each other.

1229
00:59:04,880 --> 00:59:05,980
Which was true too.

1230
00:59:06,080 --> 00:59:09,010
We have to be prepared just in case.

1231
00:59:09,010 --> 00:59:11,620
Going against Teams P1 and P3
would be too much.

1232
00:59:11,620 --> 00:59:13,850
Team Rookie is better in that sense.

1233
00:59:13,920 --> 00:59:14,920
Ji Min.

1234
00:59:15,650 --> 00:59:18,020
We're going to team up with Team Rookie...

1235
00:59:18,320 --> 00:59:21,560
because you'll become a strong opponent
if we end up in a Deathmatch.

1236
00:59:23,290 --> 00:59:25,260
- You understand what I mean, right?
- I understand.

1237
00:59:27,100 --> 00:59:29,100
"We want to team up with Team R..."

1238
00:59:29,100 --> 00:59:31,270
"because another team
might get eliminated..."

1239
00:59:31,270 --> 00:59:33,470
"from the Deathmatch,"

1240
00:59:33,910 --> 00:59:36,040
"and considering that chance,"

1241
00:59:36,040 --> 00:59:38,580
"we could win against Team R."

1242
00:59:38,810 --> 00:59:41,910
But that mindset is already wrong.

1243
00:59:42,080 --> 00:59:44,820
Why are they thinking about
ending up in the Deathmatch already?

1244
00:59:44,820 --> 00:59:46,720
Choosing the team
to play the Deathmatch against...

1245
00:59:46,720 --> 00:59:48,790
even before playing the main match?

1246
00:59:49,190 --> 00:59:50,690
It's a losing move.

1247
00:59:50,690 --> 00:59:52,260
As soon as I heard it, I thought...

1248
00:59:52,760 --> 00:59:55,630
I wanted to play this match...

1249
00:59:55,630 --> 00:59:57,060
with Team P1.

1250
00:59:57,160 --> 01:00:00,430
At the start, unintentionally,

1251
01:00:00,430 --> 01:00:02,500
a rift had formed between us,

1252
01:00:02,770 --> 01:00:04,140
and since then,
we couldn't reach an agreement.

1253
01:00:04,140 --> 01:00:06,700
After having a fallout with me,

1254
01:00:06,840 --> 01:00:08,970
Sang Min didn't seem to
want to work with me.

1255
01:00:09,110 --> 01:00:11,580
I should use this chance
to suggest an alliance with Team P1...

1256
01:00:11,780 --> 01:00:13,440
and build a good relationship.

1257
01:00:14,010 --> 01:00:15,010
Sang Min, you good?

1258
01:00:15,310 --> 01:00:16,710
(Nodding)

1259
01:00:16,810 --> 01:00:18,020
Do you want to team up with us?

1260
01:00:18,280 --> 01:00:19,420
It sounds good to me.

1261
01:00:19,420 --> 01:00:21,120
As long as my team agrees,

1262
01:00:21,120 --> 01:00:22,450
it'd be good to team up.

1263
01:00:22,450 --> 01:00:23,850
- Let's sit down and talk.
- Okay.

1264
01:00:26,620 --> 01:00:29,030
I've played a similar game before.

1265
01:00:29,030 --> 01:00:30,030
How it goes is...

1266
01:00:30,230 --> 01:00:32,230
Jin Ho, let's play together,
no reason needed.

1267
01:00:33,160 --> 01:00:35,170
- Then I'll convince my team.
- Okay.

1268
01:00:35,170 --> 01:00:36,700
- Let's work together this round.
- Okay.

1269
01:00:37,640 --> 01:00:39,740
Playing with Team P3 sounds like a plan.

1270
01:00:39,800 --> 01:00:41,210
Let's make this a perfect win.

1271
01:00:41,340 --> 01:00:43,870
Why not? There's no reason not to.

1272
01:00:44,010 --> 01:00:45,810
"Jin Ho, I'll do it if you say yes."

1273
01:00:45,810 --> 01:00:47,650
He said that, which made me happy.

1274
01:00:47,650 --> 01:00:48,980
Anyway, on the first day,

1275
01:00:48,980 --> 01:00:51,380
we had a fallout with Team P1.

1276
01:00:51,650 --> 01:00:53,750
If it happens again this round,

1277
01:00:53,750 --> 01:00:56,020
I'm worried that we'll never get
to team up with them...

1278
01:00:56,020 --> 01:00:58,820
not only for this game
but for all the upcoming games.

1279
01:00:58,820 --> 01:01:00,390
For us to decide freely,

1280
01:01:00,390 --> 01:01:03,130
we should work with Team P1 and win,

1281
01:01:03,130 --> 01:01:04,930
- and after we win, we could team up...
- And...

1282
01:01:04,930 --> 01:01:06,230
with any team.

1283
01:01:06,230 --> 01:01:08,200
Doesn't it look like the Deathmatch
will be played by the two losing teams?

1284
01:01:08,200 --> 01:01:09,630
I think so too.

1285
01:01:09,630 --> 01:01:10,900
It's still fine.

1286
01:01:10,900 --> 01:01:12,400
Even if we lose the main match,

1287
01:01:12,400 --> 01:01:13,440
we can eliminate Team P1
in the Deathmatch.

1288
01:01:13,440 --> 01:01:15,670
And I've played the equation game before.

1289
01:01:15,670 --> 01:01:17,240
Calculation is important,

1290
01:01:17,240 --> 01:01:19,010
but whether you have experienced
the game or not is more important.

1291
01:01:19,010 --> 01:01:21,580
Xitsuh, I, and Tae Gyun have played it.
That's more important.

1292
01:01:22,280 --> 01:01:24,420
Jin Ho has already made the move.

1293
01:01:24,520 --> 01:01:26,880
"We'd better team up with Team P1."

1294
01:01:27,050 --> 01:01:29,150
"And if we don't do it now,"

1295
01:01:29,150 --> 01:01:30,620
"we might completely fall out with them."

1296
01:01:30,760 --> 01:01:32,960
Thus, the alliance has formed.

1297
01:01:33,260 --> 01:01:34,260
Hello.

1298
01:01:36,290 --> 01:01:39,760
Will Team Challenger and Team Rookie
register as an alliance team?

1299
01:01:39,760 --> 01:01:40,800
- Yes.
- Yes.

1300
01:01:41,970 --> 01:01:44,100
(Teams C and R form an alliance team.)

1301
01:01:44,100 --> 01:01:46,970
From this moment, you are one team.

1302
01:01:47,410 --> 01:01:48,540
Do we leave like this?

1303
01:01:48,710 --> 01:01:50,370
- Thank you.
- We can leave like this.

1304
01:01:50,680 --> 01:01:53,080
Finally, we get to play together.

1305
01:01:53,240 --> 01:01:54,950
We get to play together
for the first time.

1306
01:01:55,080 --> 01:01:58,520
Will Team P1 and Team P3
register as an alliance team?

1307
01:01:58,520 --> 01:01:59,520
- Yes.
- Yes.

1308
01:01:59,550 --> 01:02:02,520
From this moment, you are one team.

1309
01:02:02,820 --> 01:02:05,420
Team P3 has to move out
to the outdoor survival grounds,

1310
01:02:05,420 --> 01:02:08,090
so you will be given an item
to be used for strategy meetings.

1311
01:02:08,090 --> 01:02:09,390
- Okay.
- Before...

1312
01:02:09,390 --> 01:02:11,500
the Money Challenge starts tomorrow,

1313
01:02:11,500 --> 01:02:13,330
you can communicate via these phones.

1314
01:02:13,830 --> 01:02:14,900
You're giving us mobile phones?

1315
01:02:22,040 --> 01:02:24,580
Only my team and Team P1 have this, right?

1316
01:02:24,680 --> 01:02:25,740
That is correct.

1317
01:02:26,210 --> 01:02:27,240
I got it.

1318
01:02:27,850 --> 01:02:29,950
- Let's do this.
- Sure, let's do this.

1319
01:02:30,150 --> 01:02:33,280
These two can stay together all day long.

1320
01:02:33,380 --> 01:02:35,020
But Team P3 has to go outdoors.

1321
01:02:35,120 --> 01:02:37,390
Thankfully, they gave us mobile phones.

1322
01:02:37,490 --> 01:02:39,990
We should discuss over the phone at least.

1323
01:02:40,090 --> 01:02:43,790
Team Challenger and Team Rookie
as Indoor Alliance Team.

1324
01:02:44,200 --> 01:02:47,870
Team P1 and Team P3
as Outdoor Alliance Team.

1325
01:02:48,000 --> 01:02:50,170
The teams have been finalized as such.

1326
01:02:50,600 --> 01:02:52,070
Sounds like you need to go outdoors too.

1327
01:02:52,070 --> 01:02:53,540
- What?
- That's nonsense.

1328
01:02:53,870 --> 01:02:55,410
- Come with us.
- That's nonsense.

1329
01:02:55,410 --> 01:02:57,170
Wait. Please repeat what you said.

1330
01:02:57,170 --> 01:02:59,580
- No, that's just the team name.
- Right?

1331
01:02:59,580 --> 01:03:00,910
That's just the team name.

1332
01:03:00,910 --> 01:03:03,310
It's okay.
It's worth experiencing it once.

1333
01:03:03,310 --> 01:03:04,580
No.

1334
01:03:05,850 --> 01:03:07,490
Team P3,

1335
01:03:07,490 --> 01:03:09,450
please head
to the outdoor survival grounds.

1336
01:03:09,450 --> 01:03:10,650
We're the only ones going.

1337
01:03:10,650 --> 01:03:11,860
Of course.

1338
01:03:12,160 --> 01:03:14,230
Come on, we should go together.

1339
01:03:14,430 --> 01:03:16,730
- Make sure to take care of yourself.
- Take care.

1340
01:03:17,060 --> 01:03:19,930
Her face lightened up
because she's not joining us.

1341
01:03:19,930 --> 01:03:23,270
- What's with you?
- Seong Beom, take care.

1342
01:03:23,830 --> 01:03:24,840
Have fun.

1343
01:03:24,900 --> 01:03:26,140
- See you later.
- Have fun.

1344
01:03:26,140 --> 01:03:27,200
See you later.

1345
01:03:27,670 --> 01:03:28,870
Seong Beom,
are you going dressed like this?

1346
01:03:29,740 --> 01:03:31,240
- Will I freeze...
- You...

1347
01:03:31,240 --> 01:03:32,440
Will I freeze to death?

1348
01:03:32,640 --> 01:03:33,980
- You could feel cold.
- It'll be cold.

1349
01:03:33,980 --> 01:03:35,550
Today is especially cold.

1350
01:03:35,880 --> 01:03:37,650
Does any of you know
how to use a fire steel?

1351
01:03:37,650 --> 01:03:39,320
Yes, you mean the thing, right?

1352
01:03:39,350 --> 01:03:40,480
Yes, but that...

1353
01:03:41,490 --> 01:03:43,050
How far are you following us out?

1354
01:03:43,050 --> 01:03:44,720
Tear the box thinly.

1355
01:03:44,720 --> 01:03:46,690
- Come with us.
- Come and show us how to do it.

1356
01:03:46,690 --> 01:03:48,130
Tear the box thinly...

1357
01:03:48,130 --> 01:03:49,990
- and aim for the thin part.
- Together...

1358
01:03:49,990 --> 01:03:51,360
- Or the fire will never start.
- Here...

1359
01:03:51,360 --> 01:03:53,160
We're supposed to build teamwork.

1360
01:03:53,160 --> 01:03:54,370
Shall we have a party?

1361
01:03:54,370 --> 01:03:56,900
Yes. Let's gather round...

1362
01:03:57,400 --> 01:03:59,400
- and chat.
- Sounds good.

1363
01:03:59,570 --> 01:04:03,240
We didn't have the chance
to get close with others.

1364
01:04:03,240 --> 01:04:04,980
To get closer with them,

1365
01:04:05,180 --> 01:04:07,340
we agreed right away.

1366
01:04:07,480 --> 01:04:08,680
He really likes snacks.

1367
01:04:08,980 --> 01:04:10,110
He's eating snacks all the time.

1368
01:04:10,110 --> 01:04:11,480
You don't gain weight when you're his age.

1369
01:04:11,480 --> 01:04:13,120
When I was his age, I even ate concrete...

1370
01:04:13,120 --> 01:04:14,420
when I had nothing to eat.

1371
01:04:16,490 --> 01:04:20,290
I was walking past, and the nurse...

1372
01:04:20,290 --> 01:04:21,630
This is so funny.

1373
01:04:21,830 --> 01:04:25,330
<i>Hello, it's me</i>

1374
01:04:25,330 --> 01:04:28,700
<i>Are you doing well?</i>

1375
01:04:29,130 --> 01:04:30,470
I rarely drink.

1376
01:04:30,530 --> 01:04:33,370
I don't even drink a can of beer,
but for the first time in a few months...

1377
01:04:33,570 --> 01:04:34,970
That was how I could survive here,

1378
01:04:34,970 --> 01:04:36,870
and I had to make the choice.

1379
01:04:37,210 --> 01:04:39,710
Drinking with celebrities.

1380
01:04:39,840 --> 01:04:42,550
That was a first for me,
so it was new and fascinating.

1381
01:04:42,710 --> 01:04:45,750
In the previous seasons,

1382
01:04:46,080 --> 01:04:48,820
we didn't form an alliance
to play the equation game.

1383
01:04:49,090 --> 01:04:51,490
Do we need to run around
and look for something?

1384
01:04:51,490 --> 01:04:52,860
- It's like a treasure hunt.
- Like a treasure hunt.

1385
01:04:52,860 --> 01:04:53,990
Like a treasure hunt,
you need to find the paper.

1386
01:04:53,990 --> 01:04:55,990
Don't spend too much time on searching,

1387
01:04:55,990 --> 01:04:57,260
thinking they would be hidden thoroughly.

1388
01:04:57,730 --> 01:04:58,730
Okay.

1389
01:05:01,470 --> 01:05:02,830
The rooftop... Do they know about it?

1390
01:05:05,200 --> 01:05:08,070
Tae Gyun found a safe on the rooftop.

1391
01:05:08,840 --> 01:05:11,040
(The day before,
after the Money Challenge has ended)

1392
01:05:11,040 --> 01:05:13,240
- I'll go up for a bit.
- Where?

1393
01:05:13,440 --> 01:05:15,150
Right after the Money Challenge had ended,

1394
01:05:15,150 --> 01:05:17,650
I searched the whole mansion.

1395
01:05:18,850 --> 01:05:19,880
Let's go.

1396
01:05:20,380 --> 01:05:21,690
I went around looking...

1397
01:05:22,190 --> 01:05:24,690
from the first basement floor
to the rooftop.

1398
01:05:28,160 --> 01:05:29,730
There must be something.

1399
01:05:32,830 --> 01:05:33,860
I want to find it.

1400
01:05:36,330 --> 01:05:39,170
There was a wooden box
in the smoking area.

1401
01:05:40,340 --> 01:05:41,570
There was a small gap.

1402
01:05:41,640 --> 01:05:43,740
It looked like I could open it.

1403
01:05:52,650 --> 01:05:54,180
It's a safe.

1404
01:05:57,820 --> 01:05:58,960
It's a safe.

1405
01:05:58,960 --> 01:06:00,060
(He found a safe on the rooftop.)

1406
01:06:10,730 --> 01:06:12,870
It's a safe. A passcode and a hashtag...

1407
01:06:14,100 --> 01:06:16,140
Okay. A passcode...

1408
01:06:18,380 --> 01:06:19,440
Sang Min.

1409
01:06:21,110 --> 01:06:23,310
There's a safe on the rooftop.

1410
01:06:23,610 --> 01:06:24,720
A safe?

1411
01:06:25,220 --> 01:06:26,820
Walk up the stairs to the rooftop,

1412
01:06:27,120 --> 01:06:28,990
and there's a wooden box.

1413
01:06:29,090 --> 01:06:31,690
I pushed the box, and it opened...

1414
01:06:31,690 --> 01:06:32,920
- to show me a safe.
- Yes.

1415
01:06:32,920 --> 01:06:34,260
It said to press the passcode...

1416
01:06:34,260 --> 01:06:36,130
and press the star.

1417
01:06:36,130 --> 01:06:37,460
We just need to find out the passcode.

1418
01:06:37,460 --> 01:06:41,370
If we find out the passcode,
we can open the safes.

1419
01:06:42,030 --> 01:06:43,330
One on the rooftop...

1420
01:06:43,930 --> 01:06:45,240
and one in the main hall.

1421
01:06:46,600 --> 01:06:49,540
(Another safe located in the main hall)

1422
01:06:50,010 --> 01:06:52,040
Everyone knows about the safe...

1423
01:06:52,040 --> 01:06:53,710
in the main hall,

1424
01:06:54,240 --> 01:06:56,710
but I don't think anyone knows
about the one on the rooftop.

1425
01:06:57,280 --> 01:06:59,850
Once we find out the passcode,
we can open it.

1426
01:07:00,580 --> 01:07:02,190
We should find the passcode.

1427
01:07:19,870 --> 01:07:21,570
- I'm scared.
- This is where we were on the first day.

1428
01:07:21,940 --> 01:07:23,010
Is this from the first day?

1429
01:07:23,010 --> 01:07:24,980
Yes. We ran down the hill here.

1430
01:07:24,980 --> 01:07:26,040
You're right.

1431
01:07:26,340 --> 01:07:28,980
We're back.
I really didn't want to come here.

1432
01:07:28,980 --> 01:07:31,620
Darn it, I always end up in the wreckage.

1433
01:07:31,620 --> 01:07:33,950
- Darn it.
- It's your fault.

1434
01:07:34,180 --> 01:07:36,120
I was chased out...

1435
01:07:36,120 --> 01:07:39,490
because my teammates have
bad spiritual energy.

1436
01:07:39,990 --> 01:07:42,090
(The original outdoor team in Season 2,
Hong Jin Ho)

1437
01:07:42,490 --> 01:07:44,800
The answer will be revealed soon.

1438
01:07:45,460 --> 01:07:47,660
In Season Three, who was the person
who couldn't undo the ropes...

1439
01:07:47,660 --> 01:07:49,500
and was dragged away immediately?

1440
01:07:49,900 --> 01:07:51,000
Jin Ho.

1441
01:07:51,000 --> 01:07:53,070
And who was dragged away with him
because of his choice?

1442
01:07:53,070 --> 01:07:54,140
Hye Seon.

1443
01:07:54,470 --> 01:07:56,540
Hye Seon stayed in the wreckage
for very long because of that.

1444
01:07:56,910 --> 01:07:58,410
As for Xitsuh,

1445
01:07:58,740 --> 01:08:01,380
he was abducted and had to stay there
for a long time in Season Two.

1446
01:08:01,650 --> 01:08:04,010
(In Season 2,
Xitsuh was abducted outdoors.)

1447
01:08:04,010 --> 01:08:05,250
He has been to the wreckage.

1448
01:08:06,150 --> 01:08:07,520
And he's even gone to the prison.

1449
01:08:07,680 --> 01:08:09,550
(Xitsuh: This sucks.)

1450
01:08:10,650 --> 01:08:12,490
When you're with Xitsuh
in a survival game,

1451
01:08:13,160 --> 01:08:14,360
there's no boring moment.

1452
01:08:14,360 --> 01:08:15,630
And I'm on the team too?

1453
01:08:15,930 --> 01:08:17,660
It's impossible not to end up outdoors.

1454
01:08:18,230 --> 01:08:20,800
A team composed of these members
was bound to end up outdoors.

1455
01:08:21,070 --> 01:08:23,700
We should've performed an exorcism
before we came.

1456
01:08:24,230 --> 01:08:25,640
We have bad spiritual energy.

1457
01:08:25,740 --> 01:08:27,840
Anyway, let's pull through.

1458
01:08:27,940 --> 01:08:28,970
Darn it.

1459
01:08:28,970 --> 01:08:31,110
Hong Jin Ho, the king of the wild,
is back.

1460
01:08:31,110 --> 01:08:32,940
(Hong Jin Ho roars.)

1461
01:08:34,580 --> 01:08:35,650
My king.

1462
01:08:37,580 --> 01:08:38,780
It's so cold.

1463
01:08:39,980 --> 01:08:41,420
Jin Ho, come here.

1464
01:08:42,150 --> 01:08:45,020
It has the same painting as the wreckage.

1465
01:08:46,690 --> 01:08:49,130
- You're right. They look similar.
- How did they decorate to look the same?

1466
01:08:49,260 --> 01:08:50,730
- It's scary.
- That's scary too.

1467
01:08:50,730 --> 01:08:52,200
It looks exactly the same.

1468
01:08:52,360 --> 01:08:54,360
There was a very familiar painting.

1469
01:08:54,700 --> 01:08:58,240
There's a graffiti mural
they draw every time.

1470
01:08:58,800 --> 01:09:01,840
With eyeballs, some nonsensical words,

1471
01:09:01,840 --> 01:09:02,910
and all colors.

1472
01:09:07,080 --> 01:09:08,510
What surprised me was...

1473
01:09:08,510 --> 01:09:11,050
that it looked just like the one
at the wreckage in Season Three.

1474
01:09:11,380 --> 01:09:12,720
Jin Ho and I thought,

1475
01:09:12,720 --> 01:09:15,220
"Gosh, we're sick of it. We're back here."

1476
01:09:15,620 --> 01:09:16,890
It's annoying as heck.

1477
01:09:17,320 --> 01:09:20,060
It's not the kind of hardship
you can get used to.

1478
01:09:20,060 --> 01:09:21,760
It's so...

1479
01:09:22,090 --> 01:09:23,490
You feel cold,

1480
01:09:23,490 --> 01:09:25,360
hungry, and uncomfortable.

1481
01:09:25,630 --> 01:09:27,360
It has all the bad things.

1482
01:09:27,660 --> 01:09:29,570
This is clearly our accommodation.

1483
01:09:30,030 --> 01:09:31,100
- My gosh.
- Gosh.

1484
01:09:31,500 --> 01:09:32,940
Did they sleep in the barrel?

1485
01:09:33,270 --> 01:09:35,110
- There are sleeping bags.
- What?

1486
01:09:35,470 --> 01:09:36,810
- We can use these?
- Yes.

1487
01:09:36,810 --> 01:09:38,180
- I should wear the sleeping bag around.
- They're giving us this...

1488
01:09:38,180 --> 01:09:39,510
so we won't die at least.

1489
01:09:40,180 --> 01:09:42,310
Thankfully, there were sleeping bags.

1490
01:09:42,310 --> 01:09:45,450
So I thought,
"At least they have a conscience."

1491
01:09:46,380 --> 01:09:47,550
This time,

1492
01:09:48,150 --> 01:09:49,790
there was garlic.

1493
01:09:49,790 --> 01:09:50,820
Not just any garlic,

1494
01:09:50,820 --> 01:09:54,190
but garlic freshly harvested.

1495
01:09:54,660 --> 01:09:56,290
So I was like, "What's this now?"

1496
01:09:56,560 --> 01:09:58,200
"Is this our emergency food?"

1497
01:09:58,760 --> 01:10:00,030
"Do they want us to eat this
and become humans?"

1498
01:10:00,360 --> 01:10:02,230
"Because we're beasts
if we ended up here?"

1499
01:10:02,470 --> 01:10:04,900
Did they spray water on the ground
on purpose?

1500
01:10:04,900 --> 01:10:06,800
There's a rule.

1501
01:10:08,310 --> 01:10:09,610
"Based on the results
of the Money Challenge,"

1502
01:10:09,610 --> 01:10:11,610
"the team which placed last
is sent to the outdoor survival grounds."

1503
01:10:11,940 --> 01:10:13,710
"The Ghost Casino opens once a day."

1504
01:10:18,150 --> 01:10:19,150
Goodness.

1505
01:10:20,020 --> 01:10:21,120
There's nothing much.

1506
01:10:21,220 --> 01:10:22,650
This is firewood.

1507
01:10:22,990 --> 01:10:24,920
- Burn them.
- This...

1508
01:10:24,920 --> 01:10:28,360
Honestly, when you've read
the outdoors rule book this many times,

1509
01:10:28,360 --> 01:10:30,990
you could wipe your butt with it.
You know it inside out.

1510
