- Please change them into coins.

1757
01:20:44,040 --> 01:20:46,040
- We're trading our ingredients.
- Please change these two to coins.

1758
01:20:46,310 --> 01:20:48,680
Here are seven coins equal to the weight.

1759
01:20:48,680 --> 01:20:50,850
- Got it.
- We'll bid everything on the game.

1760
01:20:51,280 --> 01:20:52,420
- It's all in.
- Okay.

1761
01:20:52,420 --> 01:20:53,580
(Bid 5 coins
for the 3rd set of Double Curling)

1762
01:20:53,580 --> 01:20:55,520
- You have bid five coins.
- Correct.

1763
01:20:55,620 --> 01:20:57,290
Please decide the order of players.

1764
01:20:58,120 --> 01:20:59,690
Xitsuh, Jin Ho,

1765
01:21:00,090 --> 01:21:02,660
Hye Seon, and then Seong Beom.

1766
01:21:02,930 --> 01:21:04,630
Why do I suddenly feel a heavy burden?

1767
01:21:05,530 --> 01:21:07,230
You shouldn't throw the stone forward.

1768
01:21:07,230 --> 01:21:09,500
Rather, slide it forward.

1769
01:21:10,170 --> 01:21:11,800
Got it. I've got the hang of it.

1770
01:21:12,670 --> 01:21:13,770
Slide it.

1771
01:21:19,910 --> 01:21:22,650
The stone has landed on minus 20
in the Counting Zone.

1772
01:21:27,520 --> 01:21:28,990
(Shocked)

1773
01:21:29,550 --> 01:21:30,890
I even got slapped in the face.

1774
01:21:31,150 --> 01:21:33,060
Jin Ho should've done well...

1775
01:21:33,060 --> 01:21:34,760
when he even slapped my face.

1776
01:21:38,030 --> 01:21:39,560
The stone has gone off the curling sheet.

1777
01:21:40,300 --> 01:21:41,870
(Eliminated)

1778
01:21:44,870 --> 01:21:47,040
Hye Seon, can't you slap Jin Ho?

1779
01:21:47,270 --> 01:21:48,940
He's crying.

1780
01:21:50,440 --> 01:21:53,380
Today's Ghost Casino is a no-go for us.

1781
01:21:54,180 --> 01:21:55,250
Can't I go again?

1782
01:21:58,410 --> 01:22:00,880
We've only got 2 more turns,
and we must aim for 50.

1783
01:22:01,850 --> 01:22:03,150
Slide it more gently than you think.

1784
01:22:19,070 --> 01:22:21,100
The stone has landed on zero
in the Counting Zone.

1785
01:22:21,770 --> 01:22:22,840
You really screwed up.

1786
01:22:24,010 --> 01:22:25,640
You really screwed up.

1787
01:22:26,110 --> 01:22:28,440
If that's how you'll end up
sliding the stone...

1788
01:22:28,440 --> 01:22:29,450
- after practicing 100 times...
- Hey.

1789
01:22:29,450 --> 01:22:30,510
Some might think...

1790
01:22:30,510 --> 01:22:32,420
- you're a national team member.
- I don't get it.

1791
01:22:33,180 --> 01:22:34,180
You...

1792
01:22:34,320 --> 01:22:36,990
What you ended up doing
is blocking the way.

1793
01:22:36,990 --> 01:22:39,720
- What am I supposed to do?
- Where should Seong Beom slide his to?

1794
01:22:39,720 --> 01:22:41,860
- He can't slide it to the middle.
- What am I supposed to do?

1795
01:22:41,860 --> 01:22:44,060
The fourth player, Heo Seong Beom.

1796
01:22:44,060 --> 01:22:45,860
(Last player, Heo Seong Beom)

1797
01:22:47,500 --> 01:22:49,170
(Eliminated)

1798
01:22:49,470 --> 01:22:52,370
Turn the lights off! Turn the lights off,
so nobody can see it!

1799
01:22:54,270 --> 01:22:55,710
You've lost the bid.

1800
01:22:55,810 --> 01:22:58,340
The bid coins are withdrawn.

1801
01:22:58,570 --> 01:23:00,740
Today's game is absurd. Seriously.

1802
01:23:00,840 --> 01:23:02,150
Who can win this?

1803
01:23:02,580 --> 01:23:05,350
We've got no firewood or fire steel.

1804
01:23:05,680 --> 01:23:08,580
Really, that curling game
was just too hard.

1805
01:23:10,250 --> 01:23:11,450
How hilarious.

1806
01:23:11,450 --> 01:23:12,820
The worst Olympians.

1807
01:23:12,820 --> 01:23:13,990
The four fools.

1808
01:23:14,220 --> 01:23:16,190
Not knowing that we were losing money,

1809
01:23:16,190 --> 01:23:17,560
we were laughing our heads off.

1810
01:23:17,990 --> 01:23:19,860
It would've been a bummer
if one of us had been good,

1811
01:23:19,860 --> 01:23:21,400
but I don't feel one bit upset.

1812
01:23:21,400 --> 01:23:23,800
What do we use the garlic for now?

1813
01:23:23,800 --> 01:23:26,570
You should eat it to get a grip.

1814
01:23:26,570 --> 01:23:27,570
Everyone got eliminated,

1815
01:23:27,570 --> 01:23:30,270
so why am I the one getting scolded?

1816
01:23:31,870 --> 01:23:33,110
- Really.
- This is driving me crazy.

1817
01:23:33,240 --> 01:23:34,610
Is this okay?

1818
01:23:35,750 --> 01:23:36,880
Either find ingredients...

1819
01:23:36,880 --> 01:23:38,650
or lay out the blankets
and get ready for bed.

1820
01:23:38,650 --> 01:23:40,920
Oh, right. Pandora's Safe.

1821
01:23:41,180 --> 01:23:42,520
On the menu,

1822
01:23:42,790 --> 01:23:45,490
the key to Pandora's Safe was one coin.

1823
01:23:45,490 --> 01:23:46,920
So we bought a key.

1824
01:23:46,920 --> 01:23:49,160
We'd like to buy the key
to Pandora's Safe.

1825
01:23:49,460 --> 01:23:51,460
Here's the key to Pandora's Safe.

1826
01:23:51,460 --> 01:23:53,100
- How cute.
- Is that the key to the safe?

1827
01:23:53,100 --> 01:23:54,160
The key?

1828
01:23:55,060 --> 01:23:57,970
Two teams were sent off into the wild,

1829
01:23:57,970 --> 01:24:00,340
and both teams opened Pandora's Safe.

1830
01:24:00,770 --> 01:24:03,840
Thanks to that,
those in the mansion suffered damage.

1831
01:24:04,240 --> 01:24:06,480
One key to Pandora's Safe, please.

1832
01:24:06,480 --> 01:24:08,380
"Exchange coins for funds."

1833
01:24:08,480 --> 01:24:10,410
"Increase in extra vote ticket price."

1834
01:24:10,410 --> 01:24:13,950
We'd like to exchange one coin
for the key to Pandora's Safe.

1835
01:24:14,920 --> 01:24:16,820
"All teams disclose funds."

1836
01:24:17,290 --> 01:24:18,290
Nice.

1837
01:24:18,520 --> 01:24:20,320
"All items' prices double."

1838
01:24:21,120 --> 01:24:22,130
Disclose funds?

1839
01:24:22,190 --> 01:24:23,630
The prices of the items rose and such,

1840
01:24:23,630 --> 01:24:24,630
which caused damage to the teams.

1841
01:24:24,630 --> 01:24:26,400
Though we may have failed the bet,

1842
01:24:26,400 --> 01:24:28,100
our plan was to find the box and open it.

1843
01:24:28,100 --> 01:24:30,970
So all of us went off to find a box.

1844
01:24:31,170 --> 01:24:32,670
- I'm cold.
- Here, catch it.

1845
01:24:33,640 --> 01:24:35,370
Oh, gosh.

1846
01:24:35,770 --> 01:24:39,210
Find the box that opens with that key.

1847
01:24:39,580 --> 01:24:41,580
Starting now, we're going
to find the safe.

1848
01:24:41,980 --> 01:24:43,010
Find the safe.

1849
01:24:43,010 --> 01:24:44,110
Find the safe.

1850
01:24:44,580 --> 01:24:46,180
Shout if you find it.

1851
01:24:46,780 --> 01:24:48,180
(Team P3 is off to find
the Pandora's Safe.)

1852
01:24:48,180 --> 01:24:49,320
Where could it be?

1853
01:24:49,320 --> 01:24:52,460
(Team P3 is off to find
the Pandora's Safe.)

1854
01:24:52,460 --> 01:24:54,220
It's hard to see in the dark.

1855
01:24:55,090 --> 01:24:56,560
From what I see, it's somewhere here.

1856
01:24:56,560 --> 01:24:57,930
Where? Over on that side?

1857
01:24:59,560 --> 01:25:01,700
This vacant house is too empty.

1858
01:25:01,700 --> 01:25:02,870
Something must be here.

1859
01:25:09,210 --> 01:25:10,270
Safe.

1860
01:25:11,310 --> 01:25:12,340
Safe.

1861
01:25:13,140 --> 01:25:15,710
Who knows what might be
inside Pandora's Safe?

1862
01:25:16,410 --> 01:25:17,480
We must find the box.

1863
01:25:17,650 --> 01:25:21,020
Honestly, I don't expect much from now on.

1864
01:25:21,180 --> 01:25:25,120
But an ice-cold Coke or beer
could be in there.

1865
01:25:25,120 --> 01:25:27,160
Or a bag of coins could be in there.

1866
01:25:27,160 --> 01:25:29,290
An item discount ticket. The best would be
an elimination immunity pass.

1867
01:25:29,290 --> 01:25:30,990
I had hopes for them.

1868
01:25:30,990 --> 01:25:33,330
Only when we find out what's in there...

1869
01:25:33,330 --> 01:25:34,730
will we know our next goal.

1870
01:25:34,730 --> 01:25:36,370
I can't find anywhere that it could be.

1871
01:25:36,800 --> 01:25:38,770
The safe isn't that obvious.

1872
01:25:41,140 --> 01:25:42,140
What?

1873
01:25:42,270 --> 01:25:43,270
Hold on.

1874
01:25:43,470 --> 01:25:44,470
What is it?

1875
01:25:44,610 --> 01:25:46,740
I found a shovel here.

1876
01:25:47,280 --> 01:25:51,980
(A lone shovel lying on the ground)

1877
01:25:52,980 --> 01:25:54,180
Maybe someone buried something.

1878
01:25:54,820 --> 01:25:56,690
No, my guess is we have to dig
something out.

1879
01:25:56,690 --> 01:25:57,990
Must we dig something out?

1880
01:25:58,990 --> 01:26:00,520
- For real?
- Where's the shovel?

1881
01:26:00,520 --> 01:26:01,890
I found a shovel here.

1882
01:26:03,360 --> 01:26:04,860
Someone must've dug
into the ground over there.

1883
01:26:05,090 --> 01:26:07,860
(Found a dug-up hole)

1884
01:26:07,860 --> 01:26:09,570
Who dug into the ground over there?

1885
01:26:12,340 --> 01:26:13,900
Why leave a shovel here?

1886
01:26:13,900 --> 01:26:14,900
(When Team R was
in the outdoor survival grounds)

1887
01:26:15,100 --> 01:26:18,070
Dig up potatoes with the shovel.

1888
01:26:18,370 --> 01:26:19,880
Dig up potatoes?

1889
01:26:19,880 --> 01:26:21,210
Dig up potatoes.

1890
01:26:22,080 --> 01:26:23,410
(Looking for potatoes
as said by Yeon Cheong)

1891
01:26:23,410 --> 01:26:24,880
I don't think that's the spot.

1892
01:26:26,450 --> 01:26:27,950
It was a stone.

1893
01:26:28,380 --> 01:26:29,890
I thought it was something else.

1894
01:26:30,820 --> 01:26:33,320
(And so,
Kwak Beom left a trace of himself.)

1895
01:26:33,890 --> 01:26:36,630
(Team P3 has gotten the wrong idea.)

1896
01:26:37,030 --> 01:26:39,800
Gosh, I don't think this is the spot.
Just look at all the weeds.

1897
01:26:41,160 --> 01:26:43,070
I only dug up a bunch of roots.

1898
01:26:43,500 --> 01:26:46,640
But strangely enough, I thought,
"Are these edible?"

1899
01:26:47,440 --> 01:26:50,340
The thought of it flashing through my head
made me hateful of myself.

1900
01:26:54,210 --> 01:26:55,980
I don't think this is the spot either.

1901
01:26:57,010 --> 01:26:58,850
While shoveling the ground,
it made me wonder...

1902
01:26:58,850 --> 01:27:01,150
if the others looked
for Pandora's Safe like this...

1903
01:27:01,150 --> 01:27:02,420
whenever it was available every day.

1904
01:27:02,720 --> 01:27:04,290
- Jin Ho.
- Yes?

1905
01:27:04,290 --> 01:27:06,320
The other two teams opened the box.

1906
01:27:06,320 --> 01:27:07,320
True.

1907
01:27:07,520 --> 01:27:10,590
That means the box should be easier
to find than we think.

1908
01:27:13,030 --> 01:27:16,200
My gut is telling me
it's somewhere around here.

1909
01:27:16,200 --> 01:27:17,270
Is something here?

1910
01:27:18,830 --> 01:27:19,840
No, right?

1911
01:27:24,610 --> 01:27:25,880
Dear safe.

1912
01:27:27,040 --> 01:27:28,210
Where are you, safe?

1913
01:27:28,740 --> 01:27:30,280
Wait, what?

1914
01:27:32,050 --> 01:27:34,520
That track looks like the forbidden one.

1915
01:27:34,520 --> 01:27:36,490
I went up a little...

1916
01:27:36,950 --> 01:27:37,950
and saw something...

1917
01:27:38,250 --> 01:27:41,060
under a spotlight...

1918
01:27:41,060 --> 01:27:42,630
as if someone was descending from the sky.

1919
01:27:47,460 --> 01:27:48,460
What?

1920
01:27:49,130 --> 01:27:50,130
- What is it?
- Did you find something?

1921
01:27:52,640 --> 01:27:54,340
I found it!

1922
01:27:54,340 --> 01:27:55,400
- He found it, Jin Ho.
- Did you find it?

1923
01:27:55,400 --> 01:27:56,840
- Did you find it?
- I did!

1924
01:27:56,840 --> 01:27:57,840
For real?

1925
01:27:58,370 --> 01:27:59,380
I found it.

1926
01:28:00,510 --> 01:28:02,350
- Hye Seon!
- I'm over here.

1927
01:28:03,380 --> 01:28:04,650
Did you dig it up?

1928
01:28:04,880 --> 01:28:06,750
- We found it!
- We did!

1929
01:28:06,750 --> 01:28:07,820
Was it... Oh, my.

1930
01:28:08,350 --> 01:28:09,520
How far did you go?

1931
01:28:09,850 --> 01:28:11,350
- Let's go. Let's go open this.
- Did you go in that far?

1932
01:28:11,350 --> 01:28:12,560
- Let's go.
- Yes.

1933
01:28:12,990 --> 01:28:14,790
Say that we open it...

1934
01:28:15,090 --> 01:28:17,260
and we are told to divide the funds
as a penalty,

1935
01:28:17,260 --> 01:28:18,730
- we're closing it right away.
- Really.

1936
01:28:18,730 --> 01:28:21,000
- I'm out of this game.
- We're closing it.

1937
01:28:23,130 --> 01:28:25,770
Our team has a lot of funds,

1938
01:28:25,770 --> 01:28:27,700
so it felt like the probability...

1939
01:28:27,700 --> 01:28:30,810
of what was inside Pandora's Safe
being bad was higher than it being good.

1940
01:28:30,810 --> 01:28:33,040
So did we really have to open the box?

1941
01:28:33,640 --> 01:28:36,350
I didn't have hopes
for an elimination immunity pass.

1942
01:28:36,580 --> 01:28:38,580
There was no way we'd get
something that good.

1943
01:28:38,810 --> 01:28:41,950
I simply prayed we didn't get something
really bad.

1944
01:28:42,550 --> 01:28:43,990
Let's pray before we open it.

1945
01:28:43,990 --> 01:28:45,250
Please.

1946
01:28:45,250 --> 01:28:46,720
- Please.
- Please.

1947
01:28:46,720 --> 01:28:48,520
- Pray...
- We went through a lot.

1948
01:28:48,520 --> 01:28:50,430
- Let's pray.
- My hands are freezing cold.

1949
01:28:50,560 --> 01:28:51,690
What do you wish it'd be?

1950
01:28:52,260 --> 01:28:53,860
- Elimination immunity pass.
- Elimination immunity pass.

1951
01:28:54,130 --> 01:28:55,430
I doubt it'd be something like that.

1952
01:28:55,430 --> 01:28:56,430
Are we asking for too much?

1953
01:28:56,700 --> 01:28:58,830
Immediate return to the mansion ticket.

1954
01:29:00,300 --> 01:29:01,640
- What a total fool.
- Funds...

1955
01:29:01,770 --> 01:29:03,310
- What a total fool.
- Funds...

1956
01:29:03,310 --> 01:29:04,510
As long as we don't have to divide funds.

1957
01:29:04,510 --> 01:29:06,180
- No dividing funds.
- I already opened it.

1958
01:29:06,180 --> 01:29:07,340
Let's see.

1959
01:29:07,340 --> 01:29:09,950
(Opening Pandora's Safe
with desperate wishes)

1960
01:29:13,850 --> 01:29:16,220
Hold on. Once you open it,
don't read it out loud right away.

1961
01:29:16,220 --> 01:29:17,720
If it's weird, close it back up.

1962
01:29:17,720 --> 01:29:18,850
What could the reward be?

1963
01:29:18,850 --> 01:29:20,890
What kind of happiness will we get
by causing trouble...

1964
01:29:20,890 --> 01:29:22,260
to those in the mansion?

1965
01:29:22,260 --> 01:29:23,830
With that in mind, I opened it.

1966
01:29:26,900 --> 01:29:27,900
What's this?

1967
01:29:28,800 --> 01:29:29,870
What's this?

1968
01:29:30,000 --> 01:29:31,000
What...

1969
01:29:32,440 --> 01:29:33,440
(Heist Day)

1970
01:29:34,840 --> 01:29:37,040
(Heist Day)

1971
01:29:37,410 --> 01:29:38,640
What's this?

1972
01:29:38,640 --> 01:29:39,640
- What is it?
- Heist?

1973
01:29:39,640 --> 01:29:40,840
I'm about to cry.

1974
01:29:40,840 --> 01:29:42,410
No, for real.

1975
01:29:42,410 --> 01:29:43,710
Another game?

1976
01:29:43,710 --> 01:29:45,920
- Please no.
- Why are you doing this to us?

1977
01:29:46,650 --> 01:29:48,550
- Seriously.
- No, please.

1978
01:29:48,550 --> 01:29:50,550
- Are we doing it?
- For real?

1979
01:29:50,550 --> 01:29:51,750
Yes, it's for real.

1980
01:29:51,750 --> 01:29:53,720
Oh, my gosh!

1981
01:29:53,990 --> 01:29:56,160
The moment I saw the word "Heist..."

1982
01:29:56,160 --> 01:29:57,430
in big letters,

1983
01:29:57,430 --> 01:29:59,960
I was about to tell the others
to close the safe.

1984
01:30:00,200 --> 01:30:02,330
Let's pretend we never saw it,

1985
01:30:02,330 --> 01:30:05,100
lock it back up,
and put it back where it was.

1986
01:30:05,400 --> 01:30:08,100
When we opened it, we saw "Heist Day."

1987
01:30:08,340 --> 01:30:11,810
There was a very familiar map.

1988
01:30:12,040 --> 01:30:14,940
It even had a guidebook for Heist Day.

1989
01:30:15,580 --> 01:30:18,580
(Heist Day)

1990
01:30:23,220 --> 01:30:25,550
Today is Heist Day.

1991
01:30:26,660 --> 01:30:29,660
For 60 minutes,
the Outdoor Alliance Team...

1992
01:30:29,890 --> 01:30:32,900
can open the five safes
hidden within the mansion...

1993
01:30:33,160 --> 01:30:35,530
and steal the funds.

1994
01:30:36,430 --> 01:30:38,300
The moment the first safe opens,

1995
01:30:38,530 --> 01:30:41,000
a siren will go off in the mansion,

1996
01:30:41,240 --> 01:30:43,940
and the 60-minute timer will start.

1997
01:30:45,840 --> 01:30:49,950
Five safes are hidden
in the Bloody Mansion.

1998
01:30:50,850 --> 01:30:53,150
First safe, the pool.

1999
01:30:54,150 --> 01:30:56,590
Second safe, the main hall.

2000
01:30:57,750 --> 01:31:00,160
Third safe, the rooftop.

2001
01:31:00,620 --> 01:31:02,960
Fourth safe, the cafeteria.

2002
01:31:04,360 --> 01:31:08,100
The fifth safe, not on the map,
is a bonus safe.

2003
01:31:08,700 --> 01:31:11,230
It becomes effective
only if the fourth safe is open.

2004
01:31:11,830 --> 01:31:13,700
Once the fourth safe is open,

2005
01:31:13,740 --> 01:31:17,110
the existence of the fifth safe
will be announced in the Mansion.

2006
01:31:18,170 --> 01:31:22,110
After 60 minutes, Heist Day ends.

2007
01:31:22,580 --> 01:31:26,120
When the time is up, only the funds
physically on your person...

2008
01:31:26,120 --> 01:31:28,080
will be counted as secured.

2009
01:31:29,550 --> 01:31:32,760
Any funds not secured
within the time limit...

2010
01:31:33,060 --> 01:31:35,460
will be forfeited to the rival alliance.

2011
01:31:36,060 --> 01:31:39,160
The outdoor alliance must do
whatever it costs...

2012
01:31:39,300 --> 01:31:41,300
to seize the funds.

2013
01:31:41,860 --> 01:31:42,900
"On your person..."

2014
01:31:43,200 --> 01:31:45,400
- It has to be on us?
- Let's see.

2015
01:31:46,140 --> 01:31:47,700
"Any and all forms of force
are permitted."

2016
01:31:47,700 --> 01:31:49,370
There are five hidden safes?

2017
01:31:49,510 --> 01:31:50,570
Five?

2018
01:31:51,470 --> 01:31:53,310
- One of them is inside...
- What?

2019
01:31:54,580 --> 01:31:56,310
"Today is Heist Day."

2020
01:31:56,450 --> 01:31:57,910
"You must do whatever it takes..."

2021
01:31:57,910 --> 01:31:58,910
"blah, blah, blah."

2022
01:31:58,910 --> 01:32:00,720
I don't exactly remember what it said.

2023
01:32:01,780 --> 01:32:02,850
(Sighing)

2024
01:32:02,850 --> 01:32:05,750
We're going to loot funds
that we don't even need.

2025
01:32:05,750 --> 01:32:09,230
The rich are trying to take more away
from the poor...

2026
01:32:09,430 --> 01:32:10,560
by pulling off a heist.

2027
01:32:10,860 --> 01:32:12,390
Why would we take from them...

2028
01:32:12,390 --> 01:32:13,460
when we have more money?

2029
01:32:13,700 --> 01:32:15,530
- Let me see. Is this the map?
- The locations are pretty easy.

2030
01:32:15,530 --> 01:32:16,570
We know where they are.

2031
01:32:20,070 --> 01:32:21,570
There's one on the rooftop too.

2032
01:32:21,570 --> 01:32:23,010
The cafeteria...

2033
01:32:23,310 --> 01:32:24,610
Was there a safe in the cafeteria?

2034
01:32:25,170 --> 01:32:27,180
Anyway, I read the instructions.

2035
01:32:27,610 --> 01:32:31,550
It said there were four safes
within the Mansion,

2036
01:32:31,810 --> 01:32:34,180
and each safe...

2037
01:32:34,420 --> 01:32:37,290
held 50,000 dollars each.

2038
01:32:37,850 --> 01:32:40,060
If we manage to get all of them,

2039
01:32:40,560 --> 01:32:42,630
the fifth safe, a bonus,
will be announced.

2040
01:32:42,730 --> 01:32:45,660
With the additional 200,000 dollars,
it can be a total of 400,000 dollars.

2041
01:32:46,160 --> 01:32:48,300
It surely is a tempting amount of money.

2042
01:32:48,300 --> 01:32:50,770
Also, the safes that we fail to open...

2043
01:32:50,770 --> 01:32:52,100
don't disappear.

2044
01:32:52,130 --> 01:32:53,700
They'll be forfeited
to the other alliance,

2045
01:32:53,900 --> 01:32:57,210
so it's not like we can stop
just because we don't want it.

2046
01:32:57,870 --> 01:32:59,980
The siren goes off after 60 minutes,
right?

2047
01:32:59,980 --> 01:33:01,710
- No. As soon as we open the first safe.
- No.

2048
01:33:01,710 --> 01:33:03,510
The siren goes off the moment we open one.

2049
01:33:03,910 --> 01:33:05,310
When we open the first safe,

2050
01:33:05,310 --> 01:33:06,980
it has the money...

2051
01:33:07,180 --> 01:33:09,320
and the hint about the passcode
to the next safe.

2052
01:33:09,320 --> 01:33:10,950
So, we open the first safe,
the siren goes off,

2053
01:33:10,950 --> 01:33:12,420
we run to the second safe and open it,

2054
01:33:12,420 --> 01:33:13,660
get the money out
and run to the third safe,

2055
01:33:13,660 --> 01:33:14,760
get the money out
and run to the fourth safe,

2056
01:33:14,760 --> 01:33:16,790
- and open the fifth one?
- That's tough.

2057
01:33:17,130 --> 01:33:19,090
But they'll definitely know it's us.

2058
01:33:19,090 --> 01:33:20,330
They will once the siren goes off.

2059
01:33:21,130 --> 01:33:24,600
How do we get to the main hall
from the pool?

2060
01:33:25,630 --> 01:33:27,100
At least,

2061
01:33:27,100 --> 01:33:28,500
Seung Jin isn't here tonight.

2062
01:33:28,500 --> 01:33:30,570
- I know, right?
- I'm glad we sent him home.

2063
01:33:30,970 --> 01:33:33,340
I'm really sorry to say this,

2064
01:33:33,340 --> 01:33:35,580
but should we just go and rest?

2065
01:33:38,580 --> 01:33:41,820
"Why? Why today?"

2066
01:33:42,280 --> 01:33:44,950
"Why does this happen to us
when we were sent here?"

2067
01:33:45,150 --> 01:33:47,560
Heist Day, Ambush Day. I hate them.

2068
01:33:47,760 --> 01:33:48,790
They sound so scary.

2069
01:33:48,790 --> 01:33:51,890
There were all those crazy guys
and strong guys.

2070
01:33:51,890 --> 01:33:53,060
None of the members...

2071
01:33:53,460 --> 01:33:55,030
were happy or thrilled...

2072
01:33:55,030 --> 01:33:57,270
about the news.

2073
01:33:57,270 --> 01:34:00,370
We were all going, "A heist? Seriously?"

2074
01:34:00,400 --> 01:34:02,470
And I felt that everyone was
reading each other's faces.

2075
01:34:02,840 --> 01:34:04,310
"A heist with this team?"

2076
01:34:04,310 --> 01:34:06,810
"No! We can't make it."

2077
01:34:06,810 --> 01:34:07,810
"Please."

2078
01:34:07,940 --> 01:34:10,050
This is driving me insane.

2079
01:34:10,350 --> 01:34:12,310
Why did it have to be the day we got here?

2080
01:34:12,410 --> 01:34:15,850
I was born to be a scholar,

2081
01:34:15,990 --> 01:34:17,820
so I've never even run before.

2082
01:34:18,050 --> 01:34:20,090
I only know how to read books
with this pale face,

2083
01:34:20,090 --> 01:34:22,160
and you want me to loot them?

2084
01:34:22,830 --> 01:34:25,160
"What if they end up taking
our funds away?"

2085
01:34:25,160 --> 01:34:26,430
"How are we supposed to loot them?"

2086
01:34:26,430 --> 01:34:28,600
It felt so hopeless.

2087
01:34:28,800 --> 01:34:31,370
If we had just one trustworthy member,

2088
01:34:31,370 --> 01:34:32,870
we would have followed their lead.

2089
01:34:32,900 --> 01:34:35,240
But we're probably the weakest team ever
when it comes to physique.

2090
01:34:35,240 --> 01:34:36,470
All those skinny...

2091
01:34:36,910 --> 01:34:38,810
Hye Seon, Seong Beom...

2092
01:34:38,970 --> 01:34:40,040
They're like this.

2093
01:34:40,140 --> 01:34:42,380
And Xitsuh is tall, but he's also skinny.

2094
01:34:42,380 --> 01:34:43,510
He's always coughing up blood...

2095
01:34:43,610 --> 01:34:45,280
and asking for his meds.

2096
01:34:45,450 --> 01:34:47,680
And I'm practically turning
into an old man.

2097
01:34:47,680 --> 01:34:49,820
I was so worried.

2098
01:34:50,590 --> 01:34:52,520
Even if you allow all forms of force,

2099
01:34:52,520 --> 01:34:54,160
we don't have that kind of force.

2100
01:34:54,160 --> 01:34:55,160
Seriously.

2101
01:34:57,630 --> 01:34:59,830
I thought, "How should we do this?
Can we actually pull this off?"

2102
01:34:59,830 --> 01:35:01,760
"But we're so physically weak."

2103
01:35:01,960 --> 01:35:04,000
- Because...
- And...

2104
01:35:04,000 --> 01:35:05,200
it has to be on us upon termination.

2105
01:35:05,200 --> 01:35:06,200
- Yes.
- We have to guard them.

2106
01:35:06,200 --> 01:35:09,070
And the main match tomorrow
requires us to run.

2107
01:35:09,070 --> 01:35:10,540
But there is...

2108
01:35:10,540 --> 01:35:12,810
one safe way that we can pull this off.

2109
01:35:12,810 --> 01:35:14,040
Just share with them?

2110
01:35:14,510 --> 01:35:15,540
We can form an alliance.

2111
01:35:16,950 --> 01:35:18,650
That's why they gave us a phone!

2112
01:35:20,050 --> 01:35:22,750
The two teams can communicate
using these phones...

2113
01:35:22,750 --> 01:35:24,590
until tomorrow's Money Challenge.

2114
01:35:27,220 --> 01:35:29,660
Only Team P1 and we have these, right?

2115
01:35:30,090 --> 01:35:34,530
(Only Team P1 and Team P3
were given phones.)

2116
01:35:34,600 --> 01:35:35,960
I had a phone in my pocket.

2117
01:35:35,960 --> 01:35:38,400
I realized they were telling us
to form an alliance.

2118
01:35:38,630 --> 01:35:39,800
We can form an alliance.

2119
01:35:41,170 --> 01:35:42,770
That's why they gave us a phone!

2120
01:35:44,170 --> 01:35:45,370
- From this moment...
- Wait!

2121
01:35:45,370 --> 01:35:47,840
Come to think of it, I heard that.

2122
01:35:48,040 --> 01:35:51,410
They said we were the outdoor alliance.

2123
01:35:51,580 --> 01:35:53,920
Team P1 and Team P3 have been
successfully registered...

2124
01:35:53,920 --> 01:35:57,350
as the outdoor alliance.

2125
01:35:57,350 --> 01:35:58,590
Are we all sleeping outside?

2126
01:35:58,590 --> 01:36:00,620
From this moment on...

2127
01:36:00,620 --> 01:36:02,790
- That's why they gave us this.
- If we form an alliance now...

2128
01:36:02,790 --> 01:36:05,490
and share the funds,
we might get all five safes.

2129
01:36:05,490 --> 01:36:07,160
They called us the outdoor alliance team.

2130
01:36:08,130 --> 01:36:09,130
- Right.
- No way.

2131
01:36:10,570 --> 01:36:13,570
"Team P1 and Team P3 are now
the outdoor alliance."

2132
01:36:13,570 --> 01:36:15,340
I thought, "Why the outdoor alliance?"

2133
01:36:15,840 --> 01:36:17,740
"Was this the reason?"

2134
01:36:17,740 --> 01:36:20,580
Plus, they gave us...

2135
01:36:21,080 --> 01:36:23,950
the antique 2G phones from the old days.

2136
01:36:24,010 --> 01:36:26,280
I thought they were telling us
to communicate through these...

2137
01:36:26,280 --> 01:36:27,550
for tomorrow's game.

2138
01:36:27,920 --> 01:36:31,050
But it was so that we could work together
during the heist.

2139
01:36:31,050 --> 01:36:33,390
The team match had already begun.

2140
01:36:33,390 --> 01:36:35,160
The indoor alliance
versus the outdoor alliance.

2141
01:36:35,620 --> 01:36:37,660
I think you're right!

2142
01:36:38,790 --> 01:36:39,800
Should we give it a go?

2143
01:36:39,800 --> 01:36:41,460
Team P1 has...

2144
01:36:42,600 --> 01:36:44,330
a baseball athlete, Keun Woo.

2145
01:36:44,330 --> 01:36:45,330
He's this big.

2146
01:36:45,670 --> 01:36:47,470
They have him, whom you can depend on.

2147
01:36:47,740 --> 01:36:49,940
Although Sang Min isn't physically strong,

2148
01:36:49,940 --> 01:36:51,540
he's a strategic thinker,

2149
01:36:51,540 --> 01:36:52,740
so he can easily control the crowd.

2150
01:36:52,740 --> 01:36:53,740
And Ji Min.

2151
01:36:53,780 --> 01:36:56,350
She has experience in this series,

2152
01:36:56,350 --> 01:36:57,580
so she'll be familiar with this stuff.

2153
01:36:57,580 --> 01:37:00,150
And Tae Gyun is a police officer,
so he'll be good at this.

2154
01:37:01,280 --> 01:37:02,450
It didn't sound so bad.

2155
01:37:02,680 --> 01:37:05,820
That means we picked the right team.

2156
01:37:05,920 --> 01:37:08,120
Team P1 is experienced...

2157
01:37:08,290 --> 01:37:11,630
and has all the stats
required for the heist.

2158
01:37:11,630 --> 01:37:13,300
Brawn, brains, and political savvy.

2159
01:37:13,600 --> 01:37:14,630
We had picked the right team.

2160
01:37:14,630 --> 01:37:17,500
We weren't picking a team
just for tomorrow's game.

2161
01:37:18,900 --> 01:37:20,700
How do I find his number?

2162
01:37:22,970 --> 01:37:24,640
Why are you turning on a game?

2163
01:37:24,640 --> 01:37:25,810
Call him.

2164
01:37:26,780 --> 01:37:27,880
I'm a professional gamer, so...

2165
01:37:32,850 --> 01:37:34,020
"Speed dial."

2166
01:37:35,650 --> 01:37:36,850
- "Alliance."
- Alliance.

2167
01:37:36,850 --> 01:37:38,290
- Should I call them?
- Yes, see if they're awake.

2168
01:37:38,290 --> 01:37:39,960
What time is it? But it's 1 a.m.

2169
01:37:40,090 --> 01:37:41,390
- Call them. They're not sleeping yet.
- I know they're awake.

2170
01:37:41,390 --> 01:37:42,420
They're probably drinking.

2171
01:37:42,420 --> 01:37:43,930
That's not good.

2172
01:37:50,970 --> 01:37:56,270
(Team P1's room)

2173
01:37:56,810 --> 01:38:01,540
(The phone is on the table.)

2174
01:38:01,840 --> 01:38:03,680
- And...
- No, what I'm saying is...

2175
01:38:03,680 --> 01:38:05,480
- we have to lie to them.
- They're not picking up!

2176
01:38:05,480 --> 01:38:08,380
If we fail, we're both going down.

2177
01:38:08,580 --> 01:38:10,150
That wasn't there before.

2178
01:38:10,150 --> 01:38:11,150
Am I able to see it only at night?

2179
01:38:11,150 --> 01:38:13,260
(Team P1 is headed to the cafeteria
at that moment.)

2180
01:38:13,260 --> 01:38:14,790
- What are you doing here?
- The pantry.

2181
01:38:21,260 --> 01:38:22,260
The person you have dialed is...

2182
01:38:22,260 --> 01:38:24,230
They must have gone to the cafeteria
without it.

2183
01:38:25,300 --> 01:38:26,840
- Should I text them?
- But it's so...

2184
01:38:26,840 --> 01:38:29,070
No, someone will read it, then.

2185
01:38:29,070 --> 01:38:31,840
We still have to discuss strategy
for tomorrow.

2186
01:38:31,840 --> 01:38:33,380
Just write, "Call me, please."

2187
01:38:34,240 --> 01:38:36,780
(Alliance)

2188
01:38:36,780 --> 01:38:42,350
(Call...)

2189
01:38:47,860 --> 01:38:51,360
(Call us!)

2190
01:38:51,430 --> 01:38:55,330
(Team P3 has a meeting
while waiting for Team P1's call.)

2191
01:38:55,630 --> 01:38:58,130
The hint for the first safe is
in the machine room.

2192
01:38:58,230 --> 01:39:00,970
We have to go to the machine room first
and open the safes one by one.

2193
01:39:01,270 --> 01:39:03,240
And Tae Gyun said earlier...

2194
01:39:03,240 --> 01:39:04,510
that he tried looking for safes...

2195
01:39:04,510 --> 01:39:06,480
and only found the one in the main hall.

2196
01:39:06,480 --> 01:39:11,310
(The safe is
at the center of the main hall.)

2197
01:39:11,380 --> 01:39:13,450
- Okay.
- Even my mom can know...

2198
01:39:13,450 --> 01:39:14,620
that there's a safe there.

2199
01:39:14,750 --> 01:39:16,220
The moment the siren goes off,

2200
01:39:16,220 --> 01:39:17,850
everyone will come to the main hall
to guard it.

2201
01:39:17,850 --> 01:39:19,720
- Right.
- That's why Team P1...

2202
01:39:19,720 --> 01:39:21,760
- Team P1 has to...
- get there first...

2203
01:39:21,760 --> 01:39:23,390
- by telling them...
- Yes.

2204
01:39:23,390 --> 01:39:24,860
that they'll guard the safe.

2205
01:39:25,460 --> 01:39:27,530
And we went to the cafeteria every day
but never found it.

2206
01:39:27,530 --> 01:39:29,160
- The cafeteria...
- It must be under it!

2207
01:39:29,160 --> 01:39:31,200
- Under the table.
- It's under the table.

2208
01:39:31,200 --> 01:39:32,230
- Which table?
- The catering table.

2209
01:39:32,230 --> 01:39:34,670
It's under the tablecloth.

2210
01:39:35,040 --> 01:39:37,310
Imagine being found out
while you're hiding there.

2211
01:39:38,470 --> 01:39:40,340
- That's terrifying.
- Wait. Is there a place...

2212
01:39:40,340 --> 01:39:41,480
where there could be a safe
in number three?

2213
01:39:42,210 --> 01:39:43,750
There is.

2214
01:39:43,750 --> 01:39:45,710
- I've never been to the rooftop.
- There's a type of patio...

2215
01:39:45,710 --> 01:39:46,920
where they smoke.

2216
01:39:47,250 --> 01:39:50,690
(Suspected location of the 3rd safe
on the rooftop)

2217
01:39:51,350 --> 01:39:53,560
The 1st and 3rd safes will be
pretty easy to hide,

2218
01:39:53,560 --> 01:39:54,660
given that we get there.

2219
01:39:54,660 --> 01:39:55,760
Numbers 1, 3, and 4 are all easy.

2220
01:39:55,760 --> 01:39:57,860
We can go straight to number 3
after taking number 4.

2221
01:39:57,860 --> 01:39:59,560
- Number 2 is the problem.
- It's number 2.

2222
01:39:59,560 --> 01:40:01,300
The second safe is a problem.

2223
01:40:01,300 --> 01:40:03,000
Come to think of it,
I have experience in this.

2224
01:40:03,470 --> 01:40:05,270
Jin Ho, do you remember?

2225
01:40:05,270 --> 01:40:07,370
- You and Hyun Seo.
- Hyun Seo and I...

2226
01:40:07,370 --> 01:40:09,270
- had a whole fight.
- Oh, your scuffle.

2227
01:40:09,270 --> 01:40:10,270
That was the spot.

2228
01:40:10,810 --> 01:40:12,940
Among all the cast members
of the Bloody Game series,

2229
01:40:12,940 --> 01:40:14,680
I've participated...

2230
01:40:14,680 --> 01:40:15,980
in the most ambushes and heists.

2231
01:40:16,140 --> 01:40:17,310
Where's Seung Jin?

2232
01:40:17,310 --> 01:40:20,020
(A member of the ambush in Season 2)

2233
01:40:20,580 --> 01:40:22,050
In the third season,

2234
01:40:22,050 --> 01:40:23,490
they hired me for the ambush when I was...

2235
01:40:23,490 --> 01:40:24,850
locked up in jail.

2236
01:40:24,850 --> 01:40:26,020
The knives are the symbols!

2237
01:40:26,020 --> 01:40:27,790
Break it.

2238
01:40:28,820 --> 01:40:30,660
(Xitsuh has a 100-percent winning rate
in breaking symbols.)

2239
01:40:30,660 --> 01:40:34,360
(And he participated in a heist
after the ambush.)

2240
01:40:38,130 --> 01:40:41,300
I have a lot of experience
in ambushes and heists.

2241
01:40:41,500 --> 01:40:43,010
But our strategy meeting...

2242
01:40:43,010 --> 01:40:44,740
was something else.

2243
01:40:45,110 --> 01:40:48,140
About halfway through the meeting,

2244
01:40:48,140 --> 01:40:49,510
they say, "Just grab them."

2245
01:40:49,510 --> 01:40:50,580
"Hold them down."

2246
01:40:50,580 --> 01:40:51,580
"Tie them up."

2247
01:40:51,580 --> 01:40:53,220
"Fight them."

2248
01:40:53,220 --> 01:40:54,650
There's always someone who says that.

2249
01:40:54,650 --> 01:40:56,720
And no one said that this time.

2250
01:40:56,750 --> 01:40:57,820
Routes,

2251
01:40:57,820 --> 01:40:58,820
timing,

2252
01:40:58,820 --> 01:40:59,920
rendezvous,

2253
01:40:59,920 --> 01:41:01,020
distraction...

2254
01:41:01,320 --> 01:41:02,920
They were such good commanders.

2255
01:41:02,960 --> 01:41:04,160
As soon as we open it,

2256
01:41:04,160 --> 01:41:05,630
the siren will go off,

2257
01:41:05,630 --> 01:41:07,830
- and someone has to be at number two.
- Right.

2258
01:41:07,830 --> 01:41:10,500
We have to guard the money here
at the same time.

2259
01:41:10,630 --> 01:41:13,340
We have to do it quickly
while everyone's asleep.

2260
01:41:13,340 --> 01:41:15,040
Hye Seon, get the money out...

2261
01:41:15,040 --> 01:41:16,370
and keep that safe, at least.

2262
01:41:16,370 --> 01:41:18,540
- And hide in the machine room.
- Then...

2263
01:41:18,540 --> 01:41:20,880
Deliver it here,
and the three of you head to the rooftop.

2264
01:41:20,880 --> 01:41:22,780
Another one holds the money
and hides here.

2265
01:41:22,780 --> 01:41:23,810
Look.

2266
01:41:23,910 --> 01:41:26,520
It was a meticulously planned,
premeditated crime.

2267
01:41:26,520 --> 01:41:27,980
(Exclaiming)

2268
01:41:27,980 --> 01:41:30,720
I thought, "I guess we'll find a way."

2269
01:41:30,790 --> 01:41:32,720
Carrying that money won't be easy.

2270
01:41:32,720 --> 01:41:34,120
- It's really heavy.
- Is it?

2271
01:41:34,120 --> 01:41:35,890
- It's so heavy.
- Should someone guard it, then?

2272
01:41:35,890 --> 01:41:37,090
It didn't feel that heavy to me.

2273
01:41:37,090 --> 01:41:38,790
Imagine walking around with it.

2274
01:41:38,790 --> 01:41:41,030
- On the fourth floor...
- But you'd have to put it somewhere.

2275
01:41:41,030 --> 01:41:43,770
We can use our hooded shirts
and tie it up.

2276
01:41:43,770 --> 01:41:45,500
Our sleeping bags...

2277
01:41:45,500 --> 01:41:46,940
Wait, we could use these.

2278
01:41:46,940 --> 01:41:48,700
We could definitely fit them in these.

2279
01:41:49,040 --> 01:41:50,140
We could.

2280
01:41:50,140 --> 01:41:53,540
Back then, it was a huge sum of money.

2281
01:41:53,540 --> 01:41:55,080
How much was it? Do you remember?

2282
01:41:55,080 --> 01:41:56,450
It was around 50,000 dollars.

2283
01:41:56,450 --> 01:41:58,050
You can definitely fit them here.

2284
01:41:58,050 --> 01:42:00,350
It might not be able to hold
50,000 dollars,

2285
01:42:00,350 --> 01:42:02,220
but it could fit...

2286
01:42:02,220 --> 01:42:03,720
if we stack them vertically.

2287
01:42:04,090 --> 01:42:05,990
I thought the important part was...

2288
01:42:05,990 --> 01:42:08,360
cooperating with Team P1,

2289
01:42:08,360 --> 01:42:10,030
opening the safes that are separated,

2290
01:42:10,030 --> 01:42:11,860
and keeping the money safe...

2291
01:42:11,860 --> 01:42:13,400
that we find in the safes.

2292
01:42:13,500 --> 01:42:15,660
We wanted to come up...

2293
01:42:15,660 --> 01:42:16,870
with a flawless plan.

2294
01:42:16,970 --> 01:42:18,400
Have you watched the "Ocean's" series?

2295
01:42:18,400 --> 01:42:19,840
They pull off a heist...

2296
01:42:19,840 --> 01:42:21,140
because they come up with flawless plans.

2297
01:42:21,370 --> 01:42:22,700
And then...

2298
01:42:23,000 --> 01:42:24,070
We need a strategy.

2299
01:42:24,070 --> 01:42:26,410
But Team P1 has to answer our call.

2300
01:42:26,410 --> 01:42:28,110
We won't be able to do it by ourselves.

2301
01:42:29,040 --> 01:42:31,110
Please call us.

2302
01:42:32,950 --> 01:42:35,550
- Five won't be that heavy, right?
- Right.

2303
01:42:35,650 --> 01:42:37,950
We needed to pull off a heist,

2304
01:42:37,950 --> 01:42:39,820
so quick cooperation was key.

2305
01:42:39,820 --> 01:42:43,890
But Team P1 didn't pick up the phone
or reply to our texts.

2306
01:42:43,890 --> 01:42:46,130
And we were worried
their phone might ring...

2307
01:42:46,130 --> 01:42:47,960
in front of everyone,

2308
01:42:47,960 --> 01:42:50,370
so we couldn't keep calling them.

2309
01:42:50,430 --> 01:42:53,300
So, we texted them to call us back...

2310
01:42:53,300 --> 01:42:54,900
and endlessly waited.

2311
01:42:54,900 --> 01:42:56,910
Sang Min is pretty perceptive.

2312
01:42:56,910 --> 01:42:59,570
They might be talking about this too.

2313
01:42:59,570 --> 01:43:01,480
That we're coming for them.

2314
01:43:01,480 --> 01:43:03,010
They wouldn't have guessed that yet.

2315
01:43:03,010 --> 01:43:04,780
- They couldn't...
- I don't think so.

2316
01:43:04,780 --> 01:43:07,180
Because Tae Gyun couldn't find
any symbols,

2317
01:43:07,180 --> 01:43:09,480
so he was convinced...

2318
01:43:09,480 --> 01:43:11,290
that there wouldn't be an ambush.

2319
01:43:11,290 --> 01:43:12,850
We talked about that during a meal.

2320
01:43:12,850 --> 01:43:14,560
Are they drinking and having a party?

2321
01:43:14,560 --> 01:43:15,790
What are they doing?

2322
01:43:15,790 --> 01:43:18,630
We're in such a rush,
and our hearts are about to burst.

2323
01:43:19,160 --> 01:43:21,400
We could come up
with the best plan there was,

2324
01:43:21,400 --> 01:43:22,600
and we'd still need their help.

2325
01:43:22,630 --> 01:43:24,530
We need Team P1,

2326
01:43:24,530 --> 01:43:26,470
but they just never picked up.

2327
01:43:27,040 --> 01:43:28,040
At the time...

2328
01:43:28,040 --> 01:43:29,100
(Kyoung Hoon is talking
in Team P1's room.)

2329
01:43:29,100 --> 01:43:31,170
That was my goal.

2330
01:43:31,210 --> 01:43:33,040
I couldn't possibly think
of going to the finals...

2331
01:43:33,040 --> 01:43:37,750
(And Sang Min is resting in his room.)

2332
01:43:46,990 --> 01:43:48,360
Where are my pills?

2333
01:43:48,490 --> 01:43:50,490
What? Do you need anything?

2334
01:43:51,630 --> 01:43:53,330
The pills that help me sleep.

2335
01:43:53,330 --> 01:43:55,500
(Sang Min gets the phone behind his back.)

2336
01:43:59,200 --> 01:44:00,600
The other team...

2337
01:44:00,740 --> 01:44:02,070
doesn't know about the phone.

2338
01:44:02,070 --> 01:44:03,540
So, it was unnecessary...

2339
01:44:03,540 --> 01:44:05,010
for me to let him find out.

2340
01:44:05,010 --> 01:44:07,980
You can't let him find out
about anything without a purpose.

2341
01:44:07,980 --> 01:44:08,980
Especially with Kyoung Hoon.

2342
01:44:08,980 --> 01:44:10,150
I just...

2343
01:44:10,250 --> 01:44:11,780
saw him there,

2344
01:44:11,880 --> 01:44:13,880
so I decided to get the phone...

2345
01:44:13,980 --> 01:44:15,080
and wait for them to contact me.

2346
01:44:15,080 --> 01:44:16,790
Because we needed to talk...

2347
01:44:16,790 --> 01:44:18,520
about what to do tomorrow.

2348
01:44:18,750 --> 01:44:20,290
So, I stayed in my room.

2349
01:44:21,160 --> 01:44:22,620
(Team P3 calls him again.)

2350
01:44:22,620 --> 01:44:24,130
It's a total of 200,000 dollars,

2351
01:44:24,130 --> 01:44:26,360
and we get as much as we take...

2352
01:44:55,220 --> 01:44:59,330
(Kyoung Hoon goes to the restroom.)

2353
01:45:02,460 --> 01:45:03,530
Please pick up.

2354
01:45:03,730 --> 01:45:04,930
The person you're trying to reach
is not available...

2355
01:45:04,930 --> 01:45:06,330
Why won't he pick up?

2356
01:45:07,900 --> 01:45:09,870
- Did you leave him a text?
- Yes.

2357
01:45:13,640 --> 01:45:15,940
(Call us!)

2358
01:45:16,110 --> 01:45:17,680
I checked it, and there was a text.

2359
01:45:17,680 --> 01:45:18,950
"Call us."

2360
01:45:19,550 --> 01:45:24,120
(Sang Min gets ready to leave
after checking the message.)

2361
01:45:24,220 --> 01:45:25,450
I think...

2362
01:45:25,450 --> 01:45:27,760
we have the worst team
to pull off an ambush.

2363
01:45:28,460 --> 01:45:30,930
Then, get some shovels, sticks,

2364
01:45:30,930 --> 01:45:32,060
and a drum can.

2365
01:45:32,060 --> 01:45:34,060
- We have to do something.
- Pick up that tire.

2366
01:45:34,200 --> 01:45:36,870
Jin Ho likes those cone-shaped chips,
so give him a cone.

2367
01:45:37,730 --> 01:45:39,730
Is there anything we can use
when we get there?

2368
01:45:42,040 --> 01:45:44,140
(Thudding)

2369
01:45:45,240 --> 01:45:47,580
Oh, man.

2370
01:45:48,840 --> 01:45:51,080
Here. I found a perfect stick to swing.

2371
01:45:52,980 --> 01:45:54,750
Do we go like this?

2372
01:45:55,920 --> 01:45:57,790
Let's go, guys.

2373
01:45:59,850 --> 01:46:02,090
Why am I always
a member of the ambush team?

2374
01:46:03,490 --> 01:46:05,030
This is my third time.

2375
01:46:06,090 --> 01:46:07,130
Hye Seon.

2376
01:46:09,030 --> 01:46:10,500
- What?
- What is it?

2377
01:46:10,900 --> 01:46:12,470
Oh, it's been so long!

2378
01:46:21,080 --> 01:46:22,110
(They got a notice in the mailbox.)

2379
01:46:22,110 --> 01:46:23,580
We got something.

2380
01:46:23,680 --> 01:46:25,010
Guys!

2381
01:46:27,580 --> 01:46:28,820
In 30 minutes?

2382
01:46:28,920 --> 01:46:30,950
"In 30 minutes,
you will leave for the Mansion..."

2383
01:46:30,950 --> 01:46:32,450
"for the heist."

2384
01:46:32,450 --> 01:46:34,520
- "Please conclude the strategy meeting."
- "Please conclude the strategy meeting."

2385
01:46:34,760 --> 01:46:36,830
Don't overthink it. We go, search,

2386
01:46:36,830 --> 01:46:38,390
throw things, and pour things.

2387
01:46:38,390 --> 01:46:39,960
Someone comes to stop us,
just swing at them.

2388
01:46:40,930 --> 01:46:42,100
Did he call back?

2389
01:46:42,130 --> 01:46:43,900
- No.
- Seriously.

2390
01:46:43,900 --> 01:46:45,970
Let's take down Team P1 first.

2391
01:46:46,630 --> 01:46:48,870
- They're a lost cause.
- Sounds good.

2392
01:46:48,870 --> 01:46:51,110
- He's not calling back.
- Gosh.

2393
01:46:51,940 --> 01:46:57,910
(He tries calling them in the main hall.)

2394
01:46:58,050 --> 01:47:01,280
Team P1 is pulling the weight
of only 2 people.

2395
01:47:01,320 --> 01:47:03,080
And we're pulling
the weight of 1.5 people.

2396
01:47:04,190 --> 01:47:06,050
- Even if we...
- Oh, we got a call!

2397
01:47:06,050 --> 01:47:07,060
Shush.

2398
01:47:09,560 --> 01:47:11,160
Hi!

2399
01:47:11,860 --> 01:47:12,990
Hello?

2400
01:47:12,990 --> 01:47:15,100
- Sang Min, is that you?
- Yes.

2401
01:47:15,130 --> 01:47:16,730
Were you sleeping?

2402
01:47:16,730 --> 01:47:17,970
No.

2403
01:47:17,970 --> 01:47:19,030
Where are you?

2404
01:47:19,030 --> 01:47:21,700
I came down to the main hall.

2405
01:47:21,800 --> 01:47:23,100
In the main hall? Why?

2406
01:47:23,240 --> 01:47:25,370
Everyone was in our room.

2407
01:47:25,370 --> 01:47:27,540
- Are you alone right now?
- Yes.

2408
01:47:27,540 --> 01:47:29,640
- Wait, let me put Xitsuh on.
- Okay.

2409
01:47:29,910 --> 01:47:31,650
- Good evening, Sang Min.
- Hey.

2410
01:47:32,050 --> 01:47:34,520
- Did you drink, by any chance?
- No.

2411
01:47:34,520 --> 01:47:37,150
How are your teammates on Team P1?

2412
01:47:37,290 --> 01:47:38,720
Our team?

2413
01:47:39,250 --> 01:47:40,920
- Are they in good condition?
- Yes.

2414
01:47:40,920 --> 01:47:43,120
Are Teams C and R asleep?

2415
01:47:43,390 --> 01:47:45,260
No, they're still drinking.

2416
01:47:45,360 --> 01:47:46,560
- They're drinking?
- Yes.

2417
01:47:46,960 --> 01:47:51,100
(Team C and Team R are enjoying
their time.)

2418
01:47:51,200 --> 01:47:53,130
- They're drinking?
- They're drinking?

2419
01:47:53,130 --> 01:47:54,640
- We...
- Let them drink more.

2420
01:47:54,700 --> 01:47:56,170
leave in 30 minutes,

2421
01:47:56,170 --> 01:47:57,940
and it's Heist Day.

2422
01:47:58,110 --> 01:48:01,210
(He tells Sang Min about the heist.)

2423
01:48:01,210 --> 01:48:02,310
Okay.

2424
01:48:04,280 --> 01:48:07,880
- We need to work with Team P1.
- Okay.

2425
01:48:08,120 --> 01:48:10,890
I think we can split the money, then.

2426
01:48:10,890 --> 01:48:11,920
What do you say?

2427
01:48:11,920 --> 01:48:13,490
I'm always down for that.

2428
01:48:14,020 --> 01:48:15,920
He said something unexpected.

2429
01:48:16,190 --> 01:48:17,560
I was going to talk to them...

2430
01:48:17,560 --> 01:48:18,590
about Equation Combo,

2431
01:48:18,590 --> 01:48:19,930
and he said, "Wait, hear me out."

2432
01:48:20,200 --> 01:48:22,230
"There's going to be a heist tonight."

2433
01:48:22,430 --> 01:48:24,430
"We're going to open a safe,"

2434
01:48:24,430 --> 01:48:26,400
"and we'll use the hint that we find..."

2435
01:48:26,400 --> 01:48:27,770
"to figure out the passcode..."

2436
01:48:27,770 --> 01:48:28,970
"and get to the next safe."

2437
01:48:28,970 --> 01:48:30,340
We're going to open the first safe.

2438
01:48:30,340 --> 01:48:31,870
And I need your team...

2439
01:48:31,870 --> 01:48:34,210
- to get the safe in the main hall.
- Okay.

2440
01:48:34,380 --> 01:48:36,380
"You and I have to stay on the phone..."

2441
01:48:36,380 --> 01:48:38,850
"to exchange our hints."

2442
01:48:39,110 --> 01:48:40,110
Hello?

2443
01:48:40,110 --> 01:48:41,580
One second.

2444
01:48:41,580 --> 01:48:43,150
- Jin Ho.
- You're breaking up.

2445
01:48:43,150 --> 01:48:44,250
- Hello?
- Yes, you can speak.

2446
01:48:44,250 --> 01:48:45,820
- Speak.
- Okay.

2447
01:48:46,350 --> 01:48:48,960
The phone kept breaking up,

2448
01:48:49,320 --> 01:48:52,860
and something big was about to happen.

2449
01:48:52,990 --> 01:48:55,360
The phone breaks up in the main hall.

2450
01:48:55,560 --> 01:48:58,570
- We'll arrive in an hour and a half.
- Okay.

2451
01:48:58,570 --> 01:49:01,500
But we can't stay on the phone
the whole time,

2452
01:49:01,500 --> 01:49:03,000
- so we'll call you...
- Okay. Then...

2453
01:49:03,000 --> 01:49:04,440
when we get there.

2454
01:49:04,440 --> 01:49:07,710
- We should rendezvous in the main hall.
- Okay.

2455
01:49:07,780 --> 01:49:09,810
I got you.

2456
01:49:09,880 --> 01:49:11,880
Anyway, they're hammered,

2457
01:49:11,880 --> 01:49:13,820
so I'm sure they'll go to bed early.

2458
01:49:13,950 --> 01:49:15,480
- Are they that drunk?
- Yes.

2459
01:49:15,480 --> 01:49:16,890
Okay, then.

2460
01:49:16,990 --> 01:49:18,350
- Okay.
- Bye.

2461
01:49:28,700 --> 01:49:29,800
Let's go.

2462
01:49:43,280 --> 01:49:44,380
It's 250,000 dollars.

2463
01:49:45,810 --> 01:49:47,020
As things have come to this,

2464
01:49:47,220 --> 01:49:48,920
- Let's earn 250,000 dollars.
- let's make it happen!

2465
01:49:49,050 --> 01:49:50,790
Let's go and make some money.

2466
01:49:53,820 --> 01:49:55,760
I guess it's a world
where the rich become richer.

2467
01:49:56,260 --> 01:49:57,890
Don't hate us too much.

2468
01:49:58,390 --> 01:49:59,960
We need to get ourselves
some weapons, at least.

2469
01:50:01,000 --> 01:50:02,560
I'm going to make sure to get one.

2470
01:50:04,270 --> 01:50:05,300
This is going to be fun.

2471
01:50:14,440 --> 01:50:15,580
What is it?

2472
01:50:23,750 --> 01:50:25,120
Listen carefully.

2473
01:50:25,120 --> 01:50:26,450
The Heist Game is going to begin.

2474
01:50:26,450 --> 01:50:28,720
And the passcode of the first safe...

2475
01:50:28,720 --> 01:50:30,530
- will be told to me via phone.
- Right.

2476
01:50:30,690 --> 01:50:34,330
The first safe...

2477
01:50:34,700 --> 01:50:35,960
Sang Min!

2478
01:50:37,000 --> 01:50:38,300
Sang Min!

2479
01:50:38,700 --> 01:50:39,800
- Hold on, Ji Min.
- Hold on.

2480
01:50:39,800 --> 01:50:42,040
Jin Ho's team will set off in ten minutes.

2481
01:50:42,040 --> 01:50:43,440
The Heist Game will begin.

2482
01:50:43,910 --> 01:50:46,570
We have to go to them...

2483
01:50:47,410 --> 01:50:49,410
and get them drunk
or make them fall asleep.

2484
01:50:49,910 --> 01:50:51,450
They will open the first safe...

2485
01:50:51,450 --> 01:50:52,780
and give me the passcode.

2486
01:50:53,850 --> 01:50:55,520
"What is this all of a sudden?"

2487
01:50:55,780 --> 01:50:57,250
"What's going on?"

2488
01:50:57,450 --> 01:50:59,750
I felt so flustered.

2489
01:50:59,750 --> 01:51:01,120
"The day has finally come."

2490
01:51:01,390 --> 01:51:02,790
"Let's make the most of it."

2491
01:51:04,230 --> 01:51:05,790
"This is insane. What is this?"

2492
01:51:06,190 --> 01:51:08,630
My heart started to beat like crazy.

2493
01:51:09,130 --> 01:51:10,670
They will arrive an hour and a half later.

2494
01:51:11,070 --> 01:51:14,100
Jin Ho's team and our team...

2495
01:51:14,340 --> 01:51:16,300
are going to come up with a plan
in the main hall.

2496
01:51:17,010 --> 01:51:19,110
- The siren is going to go off?
- Yes.

2497
01:51:19,110 --> 01:51:20,170
It will go off.

2498
01:51:20,440 --> 01:51:24,410
But they don't know we are spies.

2499
01:51:24,580 --> 01:51:25,610
They don't.

2500
01:51:25,610 --> 01:51:27,320
- "What's with the siren?"
- Right.

2501
01:51:27,320 --> 01:51:29,050
- We have to keep this stance.
- Right.

2502
01:51:29,050 --> 01:51:32,050
"What's going on?" While saying that,

2503
01:51:32,050 --> 01:51:33,790
someone should go, "Go up!"

2504
01:51:33,890 --> 01:51:35,160
Is it right to go up?

2505
01:51:35,160 --> 01:51:37,660
It won't be right to go up
if the fourth safe is upstairs.

2506
01:51:37,790 --> 01:51:40,090
We won't be going up.

2507
01:51:40,400 --> 01:51:43,100
"Go up!" The moment we say that,

2508
01:51:43,900 --> 01:51:45,770
the others will have to go up.

2509
01:51:46,100 --> 01:51:47,670
During the strategy meeting,

2510
01:51:47,670 --> 01:51:49,970
let's decide after checking
the position of the safe.

2511
01:51:50,300 --> 01:51:52,470
How do we fail our mission?

2512
01:51:52,570 --> 01:51:55,380
- What defines our failure?
- It's when we fail to open the safe.

2513
01:51:55,610 --> 01:51:57,910
Can't we definitely open the safe?

2514
01:51:57,910 --> 01:51:59,710
- They can stop us from opening it.
- They can stop us.

2515
01:51:59,710 --> 01:52:00,720
- With their bodies?
- Right.

2516
01:52:00,720 --> 01:52:01,720
That can be the case.

2517
01:52:01,720 --> 01:52:03,890
Or it can be taken away from us.

2518
01:52:04,990 --> 01:52:08,960
I think they will defend the safe
on the rooftop.

2519
01:52:08,960 --> 01:52:11,290
They know about the safe on the rooftop.

2520
01:52:12,130 --> 01:52:16,530
